	title 'Control Manager Version 3.2'************************************************************************	Control Manager version 3.2**           Copyright Apple Computer, Inc. 1986-90*                    All rights reserved*                   Written by Dan Oliver** 08/27/87 Dan - start ROMing.***	Change History:** 22 June 88	Harry Yee** The following APW files were combined into this one file.**          CMAIN.ASM*          CTRACK.ASM*          CDEFPROC.ASM*          CSCROLL.ASM*          CUTIL.ASM*          CSTATIC.ASM*          CDATA.ASM** Converted over to MAX development system.* (Version 2.5 of control mgr (System Disk 3.2))** 29 June 88	Steven Glass** Changed call table so that DragRect call would link to the window manager* when in ROM and link to a dummy file when in RAM.  Changed version* number from 0205 to 8206.** 24 Jul 88	Steven Glass** Changes made to the scroll bar def proc so that the control value* is validated before it is used.  We could make this an application* problem (as it was in the past) or fix it once and for all here.** I want to fix it once and for all.  Changes were made to scroll_init* newview and move_thumb.  In each case the control value is validated* against the values for maxsize and viewsize.  In scroll_init and move_thumb,* the value was considered correct and the MaxSize adjusted if necessary.* In newview, we assume the view and maxsize are correct and adjust the* value.** If the scrollvalue is greater than MaxSize-ViewSize something is wrong.* When we assume that the Value is correct, we reset MaxSize to be * ScrollValue+ViewSize.  When we assume the view and make an adjustment,* we set the value to MaxSize-ViewSize or 0, whichever is greater.** 16 Aug 88	Steven Glass** The routine that installs the icon font, does not save, clear and* restore the text face.  This allowed an application to have itallic* bold, outlined and shadowed scroll bars.** 14 Sep 88	Steven Glass** Started changes for Super Controls...** 28 Sep 88	Steven Glass** Change in the way that the recsize routines can use the param* field.  If the routines are called by NewControl, param is zero.* If the routines are called by NewControl2, param is pointer to* template.** Added in utilities section:**   PushStringPtr*   ReadMoreFlags*   GetColorTableRefFromTemplate*   CalcColorTableRefForCtl*** 02 Oct 88	Steven Glass** Changed a bunch of names to avoid conflicts with the window and menu* managers.  This was necessary because in the past nothing was exported* Now that the CtlMgr is in several files a number of routine names are* public.** The names that changed are**    Startup --> CMStartup*    popXbytes --> CMpopXbytes*    allocate2 --> CMallocate2*    allocate3 --> CMallocate3*    setrect --> CMsetrect*    setrect2 --> CMsetrect2** 02 Oct 88	Steven Glass** Changed kill controls to see if the control manager is active before* calling startup.  This way applications that used the* window mangager without the control manager will still work.** The problem occured when the window manager closes a window, it calls* KillControls.  When running from a system disk, this was not a problem* The control manager was not loaded if the app did not want to use it.* So a dispatch error occured and the window manager knows how to recover* from this.** KillControls now mimicks the dispatcher error.** 05 Oct 88	Steven Glass** Major changes to the dispatcher code to handle defProcs in resources* as well as new control 2.*** 06 Oct 88	Steven Glass** The active flag used by built in defProcs is in the global data* area rather passed to the defproc.  This made it hard for* custom defProcs to do the right thing when they draw.  So we also put* the flag in the hi-word of the param sent with the draw message.* This is done in Set2DrawCtl** 07 Oct 88	Steven Glass** ReleaseResource grew another paramter.** 12 Oct 88	Steven Glass** Add support for the list manager to the dispatch routine.** 23 Oct 88	Steven Glass** Zeroed ParamPtr in startup.** 24 Oct 88	Steven Glass** Modified some of the dispatcher code.  Added calls to TextEdit and* MenuMgr to find addr of defPRocs.  Simplified and shortened other * dispatching code.** 09 Nov 88	Steven Glass** Added a converter routine for code resources.  This routine is* installed at control startup time for rCtlDefProc types.  The* routine can also be used by other code to convert code resources.* A new control manager call GetCodeResConverter returns the * address of this routine.** Removed all references ReleaseCodeResource in the code.  Code* resources are just regular resources.** Changed LoadCodeResource to call LoadResource and deref the* resulting handle.** 21 Nov 88	Steven Glass** Change to TrackControl.  The ctlDrag message is different when control has* part code > $80.  If the control is a super control, the high* word of the result from defProc call is the part code to return* to caller.  This allows us to return no part code if the * user pulls his mouse out of the control before releasing* the button.** 01 Dec 88	 Steven Glass** Added call to InvalCtls.** 10 Feb 89	Steven Glass** Minor change to routines that dispatch to defProcs in resources.* These resources now need not have the high bit of their ID's set* (invalid for current resource manager).** 10 Feb 89	Harry Yee** New control message ctlHideCntl, message #18. HideControl now checks if the* control being hidden is a supercontrol, if it is then we check to see * if the FctlIsMultiPart bit is set in the moreflags field. If it is we let the * control's ctlHideCntl defproc take care of hiding the control. This is necesary * for controls that have more than one control associated with them (i.e. List Controls)** 13 Feb 89	Steven Glass** Preserved the y-reg in the new code written on 10 Feb to send* hide/erase message to multipart controls.*** 28 Mar 89	Dave Good** made the ctlHideCntl into a generic message: ctlNotifyMultiPart. Now the defproc* gets passed this message by HideControl, EraseControl, ShowControl, and DrawOneCtl* the low word of the parameter indicates which call sent the message** 28 Mar 89	Steven Glass** Added FutzCtls call.  It uses the new ctlWinStateChange message* which is now supported by all the built in defProcs.** 09 Apr 89	Steven Glass** Changed CkButton2 (used by TrackControl) so that it does not leave* mouse up events in the queue.  This could happen when button* was up before trackControl was called or if button came up after* get next event and before call to button.  Now we look at the mod* word in event instead of calling button.** 20-Nov-90	Dave Lyons** Experimenting with making the background pattern for Scroll Bar* controls a solid gray, at least in 640 mode.* Version changed to $8303.* Fixed off-by-one bug in CMDieHorribly.  Wouldn't get the "="* character in "Error=xxxx".  Won't bother fixing for ROM 3.** 20-Nov-90 (pm)	Dave Lyons** Fixed the scroll bar color stuff (was failing to set B in one path).** 9-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Changed HiliteControl(0,prevCtl) to use WaitUntil to wait 4 ticks* before unhiliting the control.** 19-Jan-91	Dave Lyons** Added 3 new calls:  FindRadioButton (returns info about which radio* button in a given family is selected); SetLETextByID and GetLETextByID,* setting and getting text in extended Edit Line controls (parameters* are window pointer, control ID and pString pointer).** 22-Mar-91	Dave Lyons** Added Compute320ScrollColor to search for a good Gray color to use* (called from NewResGuts).** 8-Aug-91	Dave Lyons** Get/SetLETextByID and FindRadioButton now accept window=NIL, to use* the front window.** 15-Sep-91	Dave Lyons** Changed CMLoadResource to force SysPrefs to always prompt for a* disk and never use a cancel button (because if we can't find* the resource, we're going to do a system death!).** 4-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** CMLoadResource now clears the supress-one-button-dialogs SysPrefs* bit, so the OS doesn't infinite-loop looking for the disk.** 8-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** Scroll bar--Compute320ScrollColor uses GetSCB instead of peeking* at SCB #100 directly.** Split some large segments into some smaller PROCs for linking into* TS3.** Changed LoadCodeResource to force OS preferences to prompt for a* disk, with no Cancel button.** 9-Dec-91	Dave Lyons** Changed Compute320ScrollColor to just ComputeScrollColor (it now* checks the MasterSCB itself).  CtlNewRes calls ComputeScrollColor.** 15-Jan-92	Dave Lyons** Having CtlNewRes call RefreshDesktop was a truly boneheaded move,* because really strange and not-goot reentrant things happen.* Instead when ComputeScrollColor changes the scroll-bar page-area* pattern/color, it uses AddToRunQ to add refreshDeskTask, which* calls RefreshDesktop(0) and removes itself from the queue.* This way we refresh the desktop on the next SystemTask call.** 15-Jan-92pm	Dave Lyons** Made CtlShutDown remove the Run Queue task, in case it got left* hanging.** 5-Feb-92	Dave Lyons** Changed version to $0303 for 6.0.************************************************************************* 3-Jun-92	Dave Lyons** Changed version to $8304 for 6.0.1d5.** Made CtlStartUp remove the RefreshDesktop run queue routine, to* avoid redrawing everything once when starting an application in* a different resolution.** 15-Jul-92	Dave Lyons (6.0.1d7)** Added new calls:*   $3C10 SetCtlValueByID(Value,@Wind,CtlID/4)*   $3D10 GetCtlValueByID(@Wind,CtlID/4):Value*   $3E10 InvalOneCtlByID(@Wind,CtlID/4)*   $3F10 HiliteCtlByID(Hilite,@Wind,CtlID/4)** 22-Mar-93	Dave Lyons (6.0.1d15)** Changed GetAndSetPrefs and SetPrefsToA to use DoSysPrefs instead* of making GS/OS calls.  This speeds up every call to CMLoadResource.** 1-Apr-93	Steve Stephenson** Changed version to $0304 for 6.0.1 (final)***********************************************************************	Blanks off	String asis		print push	print off	INCLUDE 'all.macros'	include 'equates.asm'	include 'SuperEquates.asm'myScrollPatt640	equ $00c0		;added 20-Nov-90 DALmyScrollPatt320	equ $0010		;added 20-Nov-90 DAL	include '::sys.equs.asm'	include 'e16.event'	print pop	title 'ControlCallTable';====================================================================;;          Control Manager Function Table.;;====================================================================ControlCallTable	PROC EXPORT	import WindDragRect	import FindActiveControl	import MakeNextControlActive	import MakeThisCtlActive	import SendEventToControl	import GetCtlID	import SetCtlID	import GetCtlMoreFlags	import SetCtlMoreFlags	import GetHandleFromID	import NewControl2	import CMReleaseResource	import CMLoadResource	import InvalCtls	import FindRadioButton	;19-Jan-91 DAL	import SetLETextByID	;19-Jan-91 DAL	import GetLETextByID	;19-Jan-91 DAL	import SetCtlValueByID	;15-Jul-92 DAL	import GetCtlValueByID	;15-Jul-92 DAL	import InvalOneCtlByID	;15-Jul-92 DAL	import HiliteCtlByID	;15-Jul-92 DAL		ENTRY FPTFPT	DC.L (ENDFPT-FPT)/4	DC.L CtlBootInit-1		1	DC.L CtlStartup-1		2	DC.L CtlShutDown-1	No longer shuts down (see CtlReset).	DC.L CtlVersion-1		4	DC.L CtlReset-1	Shutdown, called from WindShutDown.	DC.L CtlStatus-1		6	DC.L Reserved-1		7	DC.L Reserved-1		8	DC.L NewControl-1		9	DC.L DisposeControl-1	A	DC.L KillControls-1		B	DC.L SetCtlTitle-1		C	DC.L GetCtlTitle-1		D	DC.L HideControl-1		E	DC.L ShowControl-1		F	DC.L DrawControls-1		10	DC.L HiliteControl-1	11	DC.L CtlNewRes-1		12	DC.L FindControl-1		13	DC.L TestControl-1		14	DC.L TrackControl-1		15	DC.L MoveControl-1		16	DC.L DragControl-1		17	DC.L SetCtlIcons-1		18	DC.L SetCtlValue-1		19	DC.L GetCtlValue-1		1A	DC.L SetCtlParam-1		1B	DC.L GetCtlParam-1		1C	ENTRY dragPatch		1DdragPatch	DC.L WindDragRect-1		;Address may be patched by CtlStartup.	DC.L GrowSize-1		1E	DC.L GetCtlzpage-1		1F	DC.L SetCtlAction-1		20	DC.L GetCtlAction-1		21	DC.L SetCtlRefCon-1		22	DC.L GetCtlRefCon-1		23	DC.L EraseControl-1		24	DC.L DrawOneCtl-1		25; new calls added 20 Sep 88	DC.L FindActiveControl-1	$26	DC.L MakeNextControlActive-1	$27	DC.L MakeThisCtlActive-1	$28	DC.L SendEventToControl-1	$29	DC.L GetCtlID-1		$2A	DC.L SetCtlID-1		$2B	DC.L CallDefProc-1		$2C  (added oct 3 88)	DC.L NotifyControls-1	$2D  (added oct 3 88)	DC.L GetCtlMoreFlags-1	$2E	DC.L SetCtlMoreFlags-1	$2F	DC.L GetHandleFromID-1	$30	DC.L NewControl2-1		$31	dc.L CMLoadResource-1	$32  (added Oct 12 88)	dc.L CMReleaseResource-1	$33  (added Oct 12 88)	dc.L SetCtlParamPtr-1	$34  (added Oct 21 88)	dc.L GetCtlParamPtr-1	$35  (added Oct 21 88)	dc.L FutzCtls-1		$36  (added Mar 28 89)	dc.L InvalCtls-1		$37  (added Nov 9 88)	dc.L CMUnloadSegments-1	$38  (added May 15, 1989)*** 6.0	dc.l FindRadioButton-1	$39 added 19-Jan-91 DAL	dc.l SetLETextByID-1	$3A added 19-Jan-91 DAL	dc.l GetLETextByID-1	$3B added 19-Jan-91 DAL*** 6.0.1	dc.l SetCtlValueByID-1	;$3C added 15-Jul-92 DAL	dc.l GetCtlValueByID-1	;$3D added 15-Jul-92 DAL	dc.l InvalOneCtlByID-1	;$3E added 15-Jul-92 DAL	dc.l HiliteCtlByID-1	;$3F added 15-Jul-92 DALENDFPT	ENDP	title 'Standard Calls';;;====================================================================;	;	CtlStartup;;        	Initialize Control Manager;;  IN:     PUSH:WORD - ID to use.;          PUSH:WORD - direct page to use.;; OUT:     Nothing.;;====================================================================CtlStartup	PROCrtl2	equ 1	Stack inputs offsets.rtl1	equ rtl2+3newZP	equ rtl1+3id	equ newZP+2directPage	equ inputs	Offset to direct page (when setup).memoryID	equ directPage+2	tax	Have I already been	initialized?	bne @1	tyx	beq @2@1	brl exit1@2;	lda id,s	ID number to use.	tay	lda #RAMSIZE	Number of bytes to allocate.	jsr CMAllocate2	Allocate fixed RAM area.	txy	Pass data area handle just like Tool Loc.	jsr CMStartup;	ldy #2	Deference data area	handle.	lda [<data],y	tay	lda [<data]	sta <data	Replace handle with	pointer.	sty <data+2	jsr setWAP	Store data area pointer in Tool Locator.;;; --- Remember memory ID number to use ---------------------;	lda <memoryID	ldy #MyID	sta [<data],y;;; --- Remember direct page passed by caller -----------------;	lda <directPage	ldy #MyDPage	sta [<data],y;;; --- Clear given direct page for Dialog Manager ------------;	phd	tcd	ldx #$00FEclearDpage	stz <0,x	dex	dex	bpl clearDpage	pld;;; --- Do resolution	dependent initialization ----------------------------;	jsr newResGuts	jsl RemoveRefreshTask	;3-Jun-92 DAL;;; !!!!!!!!!!!! The following code is not ROMable !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!; !!!!!!!!!!! The patch will be done by	linker when ready to ROM !!!!!!!!!;;; --- Patch out DragRect with routine in Window Manager -----------------;	pha	pha	ldx #14+256*84	; _GetDragRect	jsl $E10000	pla	plx	ldy #NOWIND_ERR	bcs exit2;	sta >DragPatch	txa	sta >DragPatch+2;;; !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!;;;-----------------------------------------------------------;; Init the ParamPtr. (Added 23 Oct 88 SEG);	lda #0	pha	pha	_SetCtlParamPtr	pha	pha	_GetCodeResConverter	PushWord #rCtlDefProc	PushWord #%00000011		; loggin in.  system list.	_ResourceConverter	bcc exit1	cmp #$0003	bcs @NotDispatchError	pla		; clear the stack	pla	pla	pla	bra exit1@NotDispatchError	exit1	ldy #0	No error.exit2	brl CMpop4bytes	ENDP;====================================================================;;	CtlStatus;;          	Return status of Control Manager.;;   IN:    None.;;  OUT:    WORD - 1	if active, 0 if not	active.;====================================================================CtlStatus	PROCrtl2	equ 1	Stack inputs offsets.rtl1	equ rtl2+3result	equ rtl1+3	tax	Has a data area been allocated?	bne ok1	tyx	beq store1ok1	lda #6	Dan O. version number.store1	sta result,s;;	ENTRY CtlBootInitCtlBootInit		;       	ENTRY ReservedReserved		;       	ENTRY exit_toolexit_tool		;       ;	lda #0	No error.	clc	No error.	rtl		ENDP;====================================================================;;	CtlShutDown;;          	Application's call for shutting down the Control Manager.;;   IN:    None.;;  OUT:    None.;====================================================================CtlShutDown	PROC export*** added 15-Jan-92 DAL -- remove my RunQueue task	import refreshDeskTask	pushlong #refreshDeskTask	_RemoveFromRunQ*** end 15-Jan-92;; Real shut down in	CtlReset call.;	lda #0	No error code.	clc	No error flag.	rtl	Do nothing, Window Manager will shutdown.		ENDP;====================================================================;;	CtlReset;;          	Shut down Control Manager.;;  This call is what really shuts down the Control Manager.	 This call is;  performed by the	Window Manager when	it is shut down.  The reason for this;  is because many applications were shuting down the Control Manager before;  shutting down the Window Manager.  An error occurred when the Window Manager;  called the Control Manager, but found it already shutdown.;;   IN:  y/a = pointer to data area, null if Control Manager not initialized.;;  OUT:  None.;;====================================================================CtlReset	PROC	tax	Is Control Manager already shutdown?	bne ok1	tyx	beq CtlShutDown	If already off, just return.ok1	jsr CMStartup;; --- Freed data area ---------------------------------------------------;	pha	Space for result.	pha	pei <data+2	Pass address of data area.	pei <data	_FindHandle	Find handle of data	area.	_DisposeHandle	Free handle of data	area.;;; --- Set my work area pointer in Tool Locator to zero ------------------;	lda #0	Clear my saved value in Tool Locator	tay	to show I am not active.	jsr setWAP;	                  Error code returned from setWAP.	brl CMpop0bytes		ENDP;====================================================================;;	CtlVersion;;        	Return Control Manager's Version number.;;   IN:  Nothing.;  OUT:  WORD - version number.;;====================================================================CtlVersion	PROCrtl2	equ 1	Stack inputs offsets.rtl1	equ rtl2+3result	equ rtl1+3	lda #$0304	Version number 1-Apr-93 SS	sta result,s	lda #0	No error.	clc	No error.	rtl		ENDP*****************************************************************CMUnloadSegments	PROC** Unloads any dynamic segments that have been loaded* in the course of using the tool*** Inputs:*	none** Outputs:*	none** External Refs:	import Exit_Tool** Entry Points:*	none*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	PushWord #$4010	; unload all dynamics with this user id	lda #0	; file num and seg num are zero	pha	pha	_UnloadSegNum	bra Exit_Tool	ENDP	title 'OtherCalls';====================================================================;;	CtlNewRes;;          	To resolution dependent initialization.;;   IN:    Nothing.;;  OUT:    Nothing.;====================================================================CtlNewRes	PROC	jsr CMStartup	Do setup for tool call.;	jsr newResGuts	Reinitialize resolution dependents.;	ldy #0	No error.	brl CMpop0bytes		ENDP;====================================================================;;	NewControl;;        	Add a control to the control list.;;   IN:    PUSH:LONG - window pointer.;          PUSH:LONG - pointer to enclosing RECT.;          PUSH:LONG - pointer to string for title.;          PUSH:WORD - control flag.;          PUSH:WORD - current value.;          PUSH:WORD - minimum value.;          PUSH:WORD - maximum value.;          PUSH:LONG - address of control definition procedure,;	   with variation code in highest byte.;	   For standard controls the variation codes are:;	                  0	= simple button.;	                  2	= check box.;	                  4	= radio button.;	                  6	= scroll bar.;          PUSH:LONG - control's reference value, reserved for application.;          PUSH:LONG - pointer to control's color table, zero for default.;;  OUT:    LONG - handle of control.;;====================================================================NewControl	PROCcolortable	equ inputsrefCon	equ colortable+4defProc	equ refCon+4max	equ defProc+4min	equ max+2value	equ min+2cflag	equ value+2title	equ cflag+2boundsRect	equ title+4theWindow	equ boundsRect+4CtlHandle	equ theWindow+4;;	jsr CMStartup	Do setup for tool function.;	ldx <theWindow+2	Get pointer to control's window.	lda <theWindow	jsr makeWptr	windptr = pointer to window.;;; --- Ask control's defProc for the size of the control's record ---------;	stz <param	Zero the Param field to indicate	stz <param+2	that this is a call from NewControl	ldx <defProc+1	Get address of defProc.	lda <defProc	bne custom	Is it a custom control?	txy	bne custom;	lda <defProc+2	Pass standard control number.	ldx #recSize	Ask defProc for its	required record size.	jsr standardDispatch Call standard control defProc.	bra done1;custom	ldy #recSize	Ask defProc for its	required record size.	jsr customDispatch	Call custom control	defProc.;done1	pha	Save size.;;; --- Allocate the control --------------------------------------------------;	pha	Space for returned handle.	pha	phx	Size of record returned by defProc.	pha	ldy #MyID	lda [<data],y	pha	Pass ID for control	manager.	lda #0	Attributes, anywhere, anyway, baby.	pha	pha	Pass required address, none.	pha	_NewHandle	Allocate record.	tay	Put possible error code in Y.	pla	sta <Ctlhand	sta <CtlHandle	Return handle of control.	pla	sta <Ctlhand+2	sta <CtlHandle+2;	plx	Get size of block.	bcc ok1	Was a block allocated?	brl exit	If not, return error.;;; --- Dereference control's handle ----------------------------;ok1	phx	Save block size.	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ply	Get memory block size.;	sep #$20	LONGA OFF	dey	lda #0	Zero out the block.lop3	dey	sta [<ctlptr],y	bne lop3	rep #$20	LONGA ON;;; --- Hook control into head of window's control list ------------;	ldy #owControls	lda [<windptr],y	sta [<Ctlptr]	lda <Ctlhand	sta [<windptr],y	New head of list.	iny	iny	lda [<windptr],y	tax	Save.	lda <Ctlhand+2	sta [<windptr],y	ldy #2	txa	sta [<Ctlptr],y;;; --- Remember mommy window ---------------------------;	iny	iny	lda <theWindow	sta [<Ctlptr],y	iny	iny	lda <theWindow+2	sta [<Ctlptr],y;;; --- Set enclosing	RECT ------------------------------;	ldy #x2	ldx #CtlRect+x2lop1	lda [<boundsRect],y	phy	txy	sta [<Ctlptr],y	ply	dex	dex	dey	dey	bpl lop1;;; --- Set control's flag ---------------------------------;	lda <cflag	ldy #CtlFlag	sta [<Ctlptr],y	Store flags and hilited part.;;; --- Set control's value --------------------------------;	lda <value	ldy #CtlValue	sta [<Ctlptr],y;;; --- Set control's defProc address ----------------------;	lda <defProc	ldy #CtlProc	sta [<Ctlptr],y	iny	iny	lda <defProc+2	sta [<Ctlptr],y;;; --- Set control's title -----------------------------;	lda <title	ldy #CtlData	sta [<Ctlptr],y	iny	iny	lda <title+2	sta [<Ctlptr],y;;; --- Set control's reference value -------------------;	lda <refCon	ldy #CtlRefCon	sta [<Ctlptr],y	iny	iny	lda <refCon+2	sta [<Ctlptr],y;;; --- Set control's color table -------------------------;	lda <colortable	ldy #CtlColor	sta [<Ctlptr],y	iny	iny	lda <colortable+2	sta [<Ctlptr],y;;; --- Ask defProc to do any further initialization ----;	lda <min	Pass min and max as	Params.	ldy <max	ldx #initCntl	jsr CMDispatch;	ldy #0	No error.exit	brl CMpop32bytes	ENDP;====================================================================;;	DisposeControl;;        	Remove control from control list.;;   IN:    PUSH:LONG - handle of control.;;  OUT:  Nothing.;;====================================================================DisposeControl	PROCtheControl	equ inputs	jsr CMStartup	Do set up for function.;	jsr getCtlHand	ctlHand = passed control handle.;	                  	ctlPtr = (ctlHand).	bcs exit200	Null handle passed?;	jsr dispose_guts	Dispose of control.;	                  	Return error state from dispose_guts.exit200	brl CMpop4bytes;====================================================================;	KillControls;        	Remove all controls from window.;;   IN:    PUSH:LONG - pointer to window port.;;  OUT:    Nothing.;====================================================================	ENTRY KillControlsKillControls		;		      ;deadWindow	equ inputs;-----------------------------------------------------------;; The window manager can call this routine when closing; a window even when we are not active.  In the past this; happened only when the control manager was not loaded;; When it is loaded, we go to system death unless this; check is made.;; We return the old ToolNotfound error because the window; manager knows how to handle that.;	cmp #0	; see if we are active.	bne Yup	; non-zero means yes	cpy #0	; try y-reg	bne Yup	lda #1	; not active, so return tool not found error	sec	; with carry set	rtl	; and stack untouched!!!!Yup	jsr CMStartup	Do set up for function.;;; --- Dispose of every control in list ---------------------;lop300	jsr getWindptr	Get window pointer and first control.	bcs exit200	Any errors?  (y = 0	if end of list);	ldy #CtlOwner	Force control's owner to be passed window.	lda <deadWindow	sta [<Ctlptr],y	iny	iny	lda <deadWindow+2	sta [<Ctlptr],y;	jsr dispose_guts	Kill it.	bcc lop300	If no error, continue to kill list.	bra exit200	Return error.;;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	=;          Dispose control guts.; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	=;;   IN:    <ctlhand	= control's handle.;          <ctlptr = pointer to control.;;  OUT:    Carry set if error, y = error code.;          Carry clear if no error, control freed and deleted from list.;dispose_guts;;; --- Let defProc perform any disposal actions first -------------------;	ldx #dispCntl	jsr CMDispatch	clc	OK flag, just in case.	tax	Abort disposal?	bne exit100	Did defProc abort disposal?;;; --- Take control out of control list ---------------------------------;	pei <Ctlhand+2	Save control's handle.	pei <Ctlhand	It is also passed to _DisposeHandle.;	jsr dereference	sta <work	Save control's pointer.	stx <work+2;	jsr get_wptr	Get window pointer from control.	clc	adc #owControls	bcc ok100	inxok100	sta <Ctlptr	Pointer to first handle in control list.	stx <Ctlptr+2;lop100	ldy #2	Get the handle of the next control.	lda [<Ctlptr],y	tax	lda [<Ctlptr]	tay;	cmp 1,s	Is the next control	THEE control?	bne next100	txa	cmp 3,s	beq done100;next100	sty <Ctlhand	Store handle of next control.	stx <Ctlhand+2	ora <Ctlhand	bne ok101;	pla	Remove handle from stack.	pla	sec	Return error flag, control not in list.	ldy #NOT_IN_LIST	rts;ok101	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	bra lop100;;; work = pointer to	control to dispose.; Ctlptr = address of control previous to control in 'workptr'.;done100	lda [<work]	Take THEE control out of list.	sta [<Ctlptr]	ldy #2	lda [<work],y	sta [<Ctlptr],y;;; --- Free allocated memory block used for control's record ------------;	_DisposeHandle	Handle already on stack.;exit100	ldy #0	No error.	rts;	ENDP;;;====================================================================;;	SetCtlIcons;;        	Swap Control Manager Icon Font.;;   IN:    PUSH:LONG - handle of new icon font, negative for none.;;  OUT:    LONG - current (before swap)	icon font.;;====================================================================SetCtlIcons	PROCnewFont	equ inputsoldFont	equ newFont+4;;	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setup.;;; --- Return font before change --------------------------------------;	jsr pushVctl_font	Push current font on stack.	pla	Return current font.	sta <oldFont	pla	sta <oldFont+2;;; --- Change current font --------------------------------------------;	ldx <newFont+2	Use new font?	bmi exit2;	lda <newFont	jsr SetIconFont;exit2	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop4bytes		ENDP;====================================================================;;	SetCtlTitle;;        	Set new title in control.;;   IN:    PUSH:LONG - pointer to title	string.;          PUSH:LONG - handle of control.;;  OUT:    Nothing.;;====================================================================SetCtlTitle	PROCCtlHandle	equ inputstitle	equ CtlHandle+4;;	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setup.;	jsr getCtlHand	ctlHand = passed control handle.;	                  ctlPtr = (ctlHand).	bcs exit	Null handle passed?;	ldy #CtlData	Replace the control's CtlData field.	lda <title	sta [<Ctlptr],y	iny	iny	lda <title+2	sta [<Ctlptr],y;	jsr set2draw	Setup to draw.;	jsr pushPort	Save the current port.	jsr drawWholeCtl	Draw the control.	jsr popPort	Restore the current	port.;exit	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop8bytes		ENDP;====================================================================;;	GetCtlTitle;;        	Read title from control.;;   IN:    PUSH:LONG - handle of control.;;  OUT:    LONG - value in CtlData field of control record.;;====================================================================GetCtlTitle	PROCCtlHandle	equ inputstitle_des	equ CtlHandle+4;;	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setup.;	jsr getCtlHand	ctlHand = passed control handle.;	                  ctlPtr = (ctlHand).	bcs exit	Null handle passed?;	ldy #CtlData	Get pointer to control's title.	lda [<Ctlptr],y	sta <title_des	iny	iny	lda [<Ctlptr],y	sta <title_des+2;exit	ldy #0	No error.	brl CMpop4bytes		ENDP;====================================================================;;	SetCtlValue;;        	Set control's value.;;   IN:  PUSH:WORD - control's new value, 1 to select buttons and check boxes.;        PUSH:LONG - handle of control.;;  OUT:  Nothing.;;====================================================================SetCtlValue	PROCCtlHandle	equ inputsNewVal	equ CtlHandle+4;;	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setup.;	jsr getCtlHand	ctlHand = passed control handle.;	                  ctlPtr = (ctlHand).	bcs exit	Null handle passed?;;; --- Set the value	----------------------------------;	ldy #CtlValue	lda [<ctlptr],y	cmp <NewVal	beq exit	Nothing to do if already set.	sta <work	Remember old value.;	lda <NewVal	sta [<Ctlptr],y	Set new value.;;; --- Tell defProc there's a new value (draws control) ------------;	jsr set2draw	Setup to draw standard controls.	jsr pushPort	Save the current port.	jsr set2drawCtl	Setup to draw the control.;	ldy <work	Pass old value in param+2.	lda <NewVal	Pass new value in param.	ldx #newValue	Call defProc about new value.	jsr CMDispatch	jsr popPort	Restore the current	port.;exit	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop6bytes		ENDP;====================================================================;;	GetCtlValue;;        	Get control's value.;;   IN:  PUSH:LONG - pointer to control.;;  OUT:  WORD - control's current value.;;====================================================================GetCtlValue	PROCCtlHandle	equ inputsRetValue	equ CtlHandle+4;	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setup.;	jsr getCtlHand	ctlHand = passed control handle.;	                  	ctlPtr = (ctlHand).	bcs exit	Null handle passed?;	ldy #CtlValue	lda [<Ctlptr],y	sta <RetValue;exit	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop4bytes		ENDP;====================================================================;;	SetCtlParam;;        	Set control's minimum and maximum values.;;   IN:  PUSH:WORD - maximum value, $FFFF don't set.;        PUSH:WORD - minimum value, $FFFF don't set.;        PUSH:LONG - handle of control.;;              For scroll bars:	CtlData = minimum.;		CtlData+2 = maximum.;  OUT:  Nothing.;;====================================================================SetCtlParam	PROCCtlHandle	equ inputsview	equ CtlHandle+4dataSize	equ view+2;;	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setup.;	jsr getCtlHand	ctlHand = passed control handle.;	                  ctlPtr = (ctlHand).	bcs exit	Null handle passed?;;; --- Tell defProc there's a new params (may draw control) ------------;	jsr set2draw	Setup to draw standard controls.	jsr pushPort	Save the current port.	jsr set2drawCtl	Setup to draw the control.;	lda <view	Pass new view and data sizes.	ldy <dataSize	ldx #setParams	Task number.	jsr CMDispatch	jsr popPort	Restore the current	port.;exit	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop8bytes		ENDP;====================================================================;;	GetCtlParam;;        	Get control's minimum and maximum values.;;   IN:  PUSH:LONG - pointer to control.;;  OUT:  LONG - minimum value in high word, maximum value in low word.;;              For scroll bars:	minimum = ScrollView.;		maximum = ScrollMax.;;====================================================================GetCtlParam	PROCCtlHandle	equ inputsRetMax	equ CtlHandle+4RetMin	equ RetMax+2;;	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setup.;	jsr getCtlHand	ctlHand = passed control handle.;	                  ctlPtr = (ctlHand).	bcs exit	Null handle passed?;	ldy #CtlData+2	lda [<Ctlptr],y	sta <RetMax	dey	dey	lda [<Ctlptr],y	sta <RetMin;exit	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop4bytes		ENDP;====================================================================;;	GetCtlZPage;;          	Return Control Manager's zero page.;;   IN:  None.;;  OUT:  WORD - Control Manager's direct page.;;====================================================================GetCtlzpage	PROCresult	equ inputs;;	jsr CMStartup;	ldy #MyDPage	Return Control Manager's zero page.	lda [<data],y	sta <result;	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop0bytes		ENDP;====================================================================;;	SetCtlAction;;          	Set CtlAction field in control.;;   IN:    PUSH:LONG - value to place in CtlAction field.;          PUSH:LONG - handle of control.;;  OUT:    Nothing.;;====================================================================SetCtlAction	PROC	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setup.;	jsr getCtlHand	ctlHand = passed control handle.;	                  	ctlPtr = (ctlHand).	bcs errorOut8	Null handle passed?;	ldy #CtlAction	bra set_long		ENDP;====================================================================;;	GetCtlAction;;          	Return CtlAction field in control.;;   IN:    PUSH:LONG - handle of control.;;  OUT:    PUSH:LONG - value of CtlAction field.;;550=================================================================GetCtlAction	PROC	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setup.;	jsr getCtlHand	ctlHand = passed control handle.;	                  ctlPtr = (ctlHand).	bcs errorOut4	Null handle passed?;	ldy #CtlAction	bra get_long		ENDP;====================================================================;;	SetCtlRefCon;;          	Set CtlRefCon field in control.;;   IN:    PUSH:LONG - value to place in CtlRefCon field.;          PUSH:LONG - handle of control.;;  OUT:    Nothing.;;600=================================================================SetCtlRefCon	PROC	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setup.;	jsr getCtlHand	ctlHand = passed control handle.;	                  ctlPtr = (ctlHand).	bcs exit	Null handle passed?;	ldy #CtlRefCon;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = =;          Set a LONG field in;          a control record.; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = =;secondParam	equ inputs+4;	EXPORT set_longset_long		;       ;	lda <secondParam	sta [<Ctlptr],y	iny	iny	lda <secondParam+2	sta [<Ctlptr],y;exit	ldy #0	No error flag.	ENTRY errorOut8errorOut8		;       	brl CMpop8bytes		ENDP;====================================================================;;	GetCtlRefCon;;          	Return CtlRefCon field in control.;;   IN:    PUSH:LONG - handle of control.;;  OUT:    PUSH:LONG - value of CtlRefCon field.;;650=================================================================GetCtlRefCon	PROC	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setup.;	jsr getCtlHand	ctlHand = passed control handle.;	                  ctlPtr = (ctlHand).	bcs exit	Null handle passed?;	ldy #CtlRefCon;;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = =;          Return a	LONG field;          from a control record.; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = =;returnParam	equ inputs+4;	EXPORT get_longget_long		;       ;	lda [<Ctlptr],y	sta <returnParam	iny	iny	lda [<Ctlptr],y	sta <returnParam+2;exit	ldy #0	No error flag.	ENTRY errorOut4errorOut4		;       	brl CMpop4bytes		ENDP;====================================================================;;	HiliteControl;;        	Highlight/Unhighlight a control.;;   IN:    PUSH:WORD -     0 = unhighlight last highlighted	part, or draw control.;	   1-253 = part to be highlighted.;	     255 = make control inactive.;          PUSH:LONG - pointer to control.;          Current port must be control's window port.;;  OUT:  Nothing.;;====================================================================HiliteControl	PROCcontrol	equ inputsnewstate	equ control+4;;	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setup.;	jsr getCtlHand	ctlHand = passed control handle.;	                  ctlPtr = (ctlHand).	bcs exit	Null handle passed?;*** 9-Jan-91 DAL -- use WaitUntil to max out the blinking speed	ldx #0	;anticipate using 0 for DelayAmount	lda <control+2	cmp >prevControl+2	bne @different	lda <control	cmp >prevControl	bne @different	lda <newstate	bne @notZero	ldx #$0040	;delay amount@notZero@different	lda <control+2	sta >prevControl+2	lda <control	sta >prevControl	pha	;result space	lda >anchorTime	pha	phx	;delay amount	_WaitUntil	pla	sta >anchorTime*** end of 9-Jan-91 DAL;; --- Set new highlight flag ---------------------;	ldy #CtlHilite	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #$00FF	Get last highlighted part,	sta <param	and store as possible part to draw.	cmp <newstate	Is old hilite same as new?	beq exit	If the same, no need to draw.;	cmp #C_HILITE	Was the control inactive?	bne ok1	stz <param	If yes, draw whole control.;ok1	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #$FF00	Mask off present flags.	ora <newstate	Set new highlight flag.	sta [<Ctlptr],y	Put into control's record.;;; --- Draw new state -----------------------------;	jsr set2draw	Setup to draw control.	jsr pushPort	Save the current port.	jsr drawCtl	Draw the control.	jsr popPort	Restore the current	port.;exit	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop6bytes*** added 9-Jan-91 DALprevControl	dc.l 0anchorTime	dc.w 1*** end of 9-Jan-91 DAL	ENDP;====================================================================;;	HideControl;;        	Make a control invisible.;;   IN:    PUSH:LONG - handle of control to hide.;          Current port must be control's window port.;;  OUT:    Nothing.;;; Change History;; 10 Feb 89	Yee;; Added code to send erase message to multipart controls;; 13 Feb 89	Steven Glass;; Fixed y-reg for old style controls;;; 28 Mar 89	Dave Good;; cleanedup the code a little and saved a few bytes;;====================================================================Ctrl12Proc	PROC;---------------------------------------------------------------	ENTRY  HideControl	ENTRY  EraseControl;---------------------------------------------------------------;---------------------------------------------------------------tempEraseFlag	equ  1;---------------------------------------------------------------;---------------------------------------------------------------HideControl	jsr  CMStartup		;call the common startup routine	lda  #0		;add to the update region	bra  common;---------------------------------------------------------------EraseControl	jsr  CMStartup		;call the common startup routine	lda  #1		;don't add to the update region;---------------------------------------------------------------common	pha		;save the eraseFlag on the stack	jsr  getCtlHand		;get and deref the passed control handle	bcs  exit		;if a NULL handle was passed, then exit	ldy  #CtlFlag		;if the control is already invisible, then	lda  [<Ctlptr],y		;..exit	and  #Ctl_INVIS	bne  exit	lda  [<Ctlptr],y		;mark the control as invisible	ora  #Ctl_INVIS	sta  [<Ctlptr],y;---------------------------------------------------------------	ldy  #NewCtlRecord.CtlProc+2	;is this a super control ? If not, then	lda  [<Ctlptr],y		;..we never need to notify this ctrl	bpl  skipNotify	ldy  #NewCtlRecord.ctlMoreFlags	;does this defProc want this message ?	lda  [<Ctlptr],y	and  #fCtlIsMultiPart	beq  skipNotify		lda  tempEraseFlag,s	ldy  #0	ldx  #ctlNotifyMultiPart	jsr  CMDispatchskipNotify;---------------------------------------------------------------	jsr  to_wport		;switch to control's window port.	jsr  CMsetrect		;'rect' = control's enclosing RECT.	ldy  #ctlProc		;is the control a simple button ? If not	lda  [<ctlptr],y		;..then don't expand the rect	iny	ora  [<ctlptr],y	bne  @skipButton	ldy  #CtlFlag		;does the button need it's rect expanded ?	lda  [<ctlptr],y		;..nope = skip expand	and  #1	beq  @skipButton	jsr  expandButt		;expand 'rect' to include bold.@skipButton	jsr  pushrect		;erase the control	_EraseRect	lda  tempEraseFlag,s	;do we need to invalidate the control ?	bne  @skipInval	jsr  pushrect		;invalidate the control	_InvalRect@skipInval;---------------------------------------------------------------exit	pla		;pull off the erase flag	ldy  #0		;return no error	brl  CMpop4bytes;---------------------------------------------------------------	ENDP;====================================================================;;	ShowControl & DrawOneCtl;;        	Make a control visible.;;   IN:    PUSH:LONG - handle of control to make visible (or draw).;          Current port must be control's window port.;;  OUT:    Nothing.;;; Change History;; 28 Mar 89	Dave Good;; Combined show and draw one control to save space. Also made both of them; call the defProc for multi part controls.;;====================================================================Ctrl2Proc	PROC;---------------------------------------------------------------	ENTRY  DrawOneCtl	ENTRY  ShowControl;---------------------------------------------------------------;---------------------------------------------------------------DrawOneCtl	jsr  CMStartup		;call the common startup routine	jsr  getCtlHand		;get and deref the passed control handle	bcs  exit		;if a NULL handle was passed, then exit	ldx  #3	bra  drawIt;---------------------------------------------------------------ShowControl	jsr  CMStartup		;call the common startup routine	jsr  getCtlHand		;get and deref the passed control handle	bcs  exit		;if a NULL handle was passed, then exit	ldy  #CtlFlag		;if the control is already visible then	lda  [<Ctlptr],y		;..exit	and  #Ctl_INVIS	beq  exit	lda  [<Ctlptr],y		;it was not visible before, so make it	and  #$FF7F		;..visible	sta  [<Ctlptr],y	ldx  #2		;this is what param to send;---------------------------------------------------------------drawIt	ldy  #NewCtlRecord.CtlProc+2	;is this a super control ? If not, then	lda  [<Ctlptr],y		;..we never need to notify this ctrl	bpl  skipNotify	ldy  #NewCtlRecord.ctlMoreFlags	;does this defProc want this message ?	lda  [<Ctlptr],y	and  #fCtlIsMultiPart	beq  skipNotify		txa		;this tells the defproc to show the	ldy  #0		;..control	ldx  #ctlNotifyMultiPart	jsr  CMDispatchskipNotify;---------------------------------------------------------------	jsr  set2draw		;setup to draw control.	jsr  pushPort		;save the current port.	jsr  drawWholeCtl		;draw the control.	jsr  popPort		;restore the current port.exit	ldy  #0		;no error flag.	brl  CMpop4bytes;---------------------------------------------------------------		ENDP;====================================================================;;	DrawControls;;        	Draw control list.;;   IN:    PUSH:LONG - pointer to window.;;  OUT:    Nothing.;;          Will just exit if a null window pointer passed or no controls;          in window's control list.;;====================================================================DrawControls	PROCwindow	equ inputscount	equ window+4;yoffset	equ workxoffset	equ yoffset+2;;	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setup.;	jsr getWindPtr	Get given window pointer.	bcs exit	Any errors?;	ldy #owFrame	Is window visible?	lda [<windptr],y	and #F_VIS	beq exit	Nothing to draw if invisible.;	jsr set2draw	Switch to CtlOwner port, get visBounds.	jsr pushPort	Save the current port.;;; --- Draw all the controls in the list	--------------;lop1	jsr drawWholeCtl	Do standard setups,	and draw control.;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).;	jsr next_Ctl	Get pointer to next	control.	bne lop1	Any more controls?;	jsr popPort	Restore the current	port.;exit	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop4bytes		ENDP;====================================================================;;	InvalCtls;;        	Invalidates bound rects of the controls in the window;;   IN:    PUSH:LONG - pointer to window.;;  OUT:    Nothing.;;          Will just exit if a null window pointer passed or no controls;          in window's control list.;;====================================================================InvalCtls 	PROCwindow	equ inputs;;	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setup.;	jsr getWindPtr	Get given window pointer.	bcs exit	Any errors?;	ldy #owFrame	Is window visible?	lda [<windptr],y	and #F_VIS	beq exit	Nothing to do if invisible.	pha	pha	_GetPort	pei Window+2	pei Window	_SetPort	pha	pha	pha	pha	tsc	inc a	pea 0	pha	_GetPortRect	pei Window+2	pei Window	_StartDrawing;;; --- Invalidate all the controls in the list --------------;lop1	lda ctlPtr	clc	adc #NewCtlRecord.ctlRect	tax	lda ctlPtr+2	adc #0	pha	phx	_InvalRect;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).;	jsr next_Ctl	Get pointer to next	control.	bne lop1	Any more controls?	_SetOrigin	pla	pla;	_SetPort	Restore orig port.;exit	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop4bytes		ENDP;====================================================================;;	FutzCtls;; Invalidates bound rects of normal controls in the window and; sends message to other controls telling that window state has; changed.;; This call is supposed to be made in reponse to a activate event; so the state of the controls can be tied to the window state.;;   IN:    PUSH:LONG - pointer to window.;          PUSH:WORD - Window State;;  OUT:    Nothing.;;          Will just exit if a null window pointer passed or no controls;          in window's control list.;;====================================================================FutzCtls	PROCwindow	equ inputswindowState	equ window+4;;	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setup.;	jsr getWindPtr	Get given window pointer.	bcs exit	Any errors?;	ldy #owFrame	Is window visible?	lda [<windptr],y	and #F_VIS	beq exit	Nothing to do if invisible.	pha	pha	_GetPort	pei Window+2	pei Window	_SetPort	pha	pha	pha	pha	tsc	inc a	pea 0	pha	_GetPortRect	pei Window+2	pei Window	_StartDrawing;;; --- Invalidate all the controls in the list --------------;lop1	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlProc+2	lda [<ctlPtr],y	bmi ItsSuper	lda ctlPtr	clc	adc #NewCtlRecord.ctlRect	tax	lda ctlPtr+2	adc #0	pha	phx	_InvalRect	bra JoinUp;ItsSuper	lda WindowState		; notify this def proc.	ldy #0	ldx #ctlWinStateChange	jsr CMDispatchJoinUp	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).;	jsr next_Ctl	Get pointer to next	control.	bne lop1	Any more controls?	_SetOrigin	pla	pla;	_SetPort	Restore orig port.;exit	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop6bytes		ENDP************************************************************************ $3910 FindRadioButton -- added 19-Jan-91 DAL** This routine is compatible with the fmdWhichRadio call in the* DTS FakeModalDialog user toolset (original code by Eric Soldan).** Inputs:*   Space for result (WORD)*   Window Pointer   (LONG)*   Family Number    (WORD)** Given the family number of a family of extended radio button controls* in the specified window, we determine which radio button in the family* is selected, and the return value is the selected button's control ID* MINUS the control ID of the lowest-ID'ed control in the family.***********************************************************************FindRadioButton	proc export; offset constants for CtlRecoctlNext	equ 0octlOwner	equ 4octlRect	equ 8octlFlag	equ 16octlHilite	equ 17octlValue	equ 18octlProc	equ 20octlAction	equ 24octlData	equ 28octlRefCon	equ 32octlColor	equ 36octlReserved	equ 40octlID	equ 56octlMoreFlags	equ 60octlVersion	equ 62	DefineStackctlHndl	long	;Must be at 1,srbCtlPtr	longctlID	long	;ID of some radio button control.theRadBut	wordnotHere	word	;Flag for active button not found.sizeLocals	EndLocalssaveDPage	wordreturnAddr	block 6	;was block 3 (DAL)	BegParmsfamNum	wordwptr	long	;Window that owns the control.sizeParms	EndParmsradioNum	word	phd	;Save directPage register.	tsc	;Make space for locals.	sec	sbc #sizeLocals	tcs	tcd	;Set directPage register.	lda #$FFFF	;This is supposed to be a bogus value	sta radioNum	;(0 is legit).	sta notHere	;Assume we won't find active radio	sta ctlID+2	;button of correct family number.*** added 8-Aug-91 DAL, to handle window-pointer = NIL --> front window	lda <wptr+1	bne @notNIL	pha	pha	_FrontWindow	pla	sta <wptr	pla	sta <wptr+2@notNIL*** end 8-Aug-91 DAL	pei wptr+2	pei wptr	_GetWControls	;Result space already there (ctlHndl).	bcs @exit@loop	lda ctlHndl+1	;See if we have a NULL handle yet.	beq @endLoop	jsr @derefCtl	;Deref ctlHndl into rbCtlPtr.	ldy #octlProc+2	;Get hi-word of proc address.	lda [rbCtlPtr],y	cmp #radioControl>>16	bne @nextCtl	;Not a radio button.  Skip it.	ldy #octlFlag	lda [rbCtlPtr],y	and #$7F	cmp famNum	;See if it is "our" family.	bne @nextCtl	;Not related.	ldy #octlID+2	;See if this is the smallest ctlID for	lda [rbCtlPtr],y	;our family yet.	tax	dey	dey	lda [rbCtlPtr],y	cpx ctlID+2	bcc @smaller	bne @a	;It isn't.	cmp ctlID	bcs @a	;It isn't.@smaller	sta ctlID	;It is, so remember it.	stx ctlID+2@a	tax	ldy #octlValue	lda [rbCtlPtr],y	beq @nextCtl	;This isn't the active radio button.	stx theRadBut	;This is the one, so remember enough	stz notHere	;of it.  Also, flag we found it.@nextCtl	ldy #2	lda [rbCtlPtr]	sta ctlHndl	lda [rbCtlPtr],y	sta ctlHndl+2	bra @loop@endLoop	lda notHere	;See if we found it.  If we didn't,	bmi @b	;return $FFFF to indicate this.	lda theRadBut	sec	sbc ctlID@b	sta radioNum	;This is what the programmer was		;yearning for.	lda #0	;Return no error.@exit	tax	;save error code in X	tdc	;Get rid of local variables.	clc	adc #sizeLocals	tcs	pld	;Restore directPage register.	ldy #sizeParms	;error already in X	jml $e10184	;ToStrip@derefCtl	ldy #2	lda [ctlHndl]	sta rbCtlPtr	lda [ctlHndl],y	sta rbCtlPtr+2	rts	ENDP************************************************************************ $3A10 SetLETextByID -- added 19-Jan-91 DAL** This routine is compatible with the fmdLESetText call in the* DTS FakeModalDialog user toolset (original code by Eric Soldan).** Inputs:*   Window Pointer        (LONG)*   Edit Line Control ID  (LONG)*   Pascal String Pointer (LONG)** Given the control ID of an extended edit line control in the* specified window, we set its text from the Pascal string, thus* saving the application programmer having to call GetCtlHandleFromID,* GetCtlTitle, and LESetText, plus some miscellaneous string* manipulation and handle dereferencing.** This routine *selects* the text it puts into the Edit Line control.***********************************************************************SetLETextByID	proc export	export GetLETextByID; offset constants for LERecoleLineHandle	equ 0oleLength	equ 4oleMaxLength	equ 6oleDestRect	equ 8oleViewRect	equ 16olePort	equ 24oleLineHite	equ 28oleBaseHite	equ 30oleSelStart	equ 32oleSelEnd	equ 34oleActFlg	equ 36oleCarAct	equ 38oleCarOn	equ 40oleCarTime	equ 42oleHiliteHook	equ 46oleCaretHook	equ 50oleJust	equ 54olePWChar	equ 56; from E16.ControloctlData	equ 28	DefineStackctlHndl	longleCtlPtr	longleHndl	longlePtr	longlineHndl	longlinePtr	longcstr	longlineLength	wordleRect	block 8	;Must be > oleViewRect ($10)sizeLocals	EndLocalssaveDPage	wordreturnAddr	block 6	;was block 3 (DAL)	BegParmspstr	long	;Pointer to string space.lineEditID	long	;ID of lineEdit control.wptr	long	;Window that owns the control.sizeParms	EndParms** SetLETextByID*	jsr lineEditSetup	;Set up everything we need.	bcs exit	;Couldn't dereference for some reason.	pei cstr+2	;Set text to c-string.	pei cstr	lda [pstr]	;Get length of pascal string.	and #$00FF	pha	pei leHndl+2	pei leHndl	_LESetText	bcs exit	pha	;Invalidate view rect of lineEdit.	pha	_GetPort	;Save the current port.	pei wptr+2	pei wptr	_SetPort	;Make the window the current port		;(for _InvalRect).	jsr lineEditDeref	;Redereference -- slow but small.	ldy #oleSelStart	lda #0	pha	;Hi-word for _InvalRect.	sta [lePtr],y	iny	iny	;Point at leSelEnd.	lda [pstr]	;Get length of pascal string.	and #$00FF	sta [lePtr],y	ldy #oleViewRect+6	;Copy lineEdit viewRect into rect.@a	lda [lePtr],y	tyx	sta <leRect-oleViewRect,x	dey	dey	cpy #oleViewRect	bcs @a	tdc	;Hi-word alreay on stack.  (It's a 0).	adc #leRect	;Carry still clear.	pha	_InvalRect	;Inval that rect.	_SetPort	;Put the port back.exitNoErr	lda #0	;Return no error.exit	tax	;Save error code.	tdc	;Get rid of local variables.	clc	adc #sizeLocals	tcs	pld	;Restore directPage register.	ldy #sizeParms	jml $e10184	;ToStrip************************************************************************ $3B10 GetLETextByID -- added 19-Jan-91 DAL** This routine is compatible with the fmdLESetText call in the* DTS FakeModalDialog user toolset (original code by Eric Soldan).** Inputs:*   Window Pointer        (LONG)*   Edit Line Control ID  (LONG)*   Pascal String Pointer (LONG)** Given the control ID of an extended edit line control in the* specified window, we fetch its text into the Pascal string, thus* saving the application programmer having to call GetCtlHandleFromID,* GetCtlTitle, LEGetTextHand, LEGetTextLen, and doing miscellaneous* string manipulation and handle dereferencing.***********************************************************************GetLETextByID	jsr lineEditSetup	;Set up everything we need.	bcs exit	;Couldn't dereference for some reason.	pei linePtr+2	;Copy the text into the string.	pei linePtr	pei cstr+2	pei cstr	pea 0	pei lineLength	_BlockMove	ldy lineLength	;Store the p-string length and also	tya	;terminate the string for the c dudes.	shortm	;Use 8-bit accumulator.	sta [pstr]	;Save the p-string length byte.	lda #0	sta [cstr],y	;Terminate the c-string.	longm	;Set accumulator back to 16-bit.	bra exitNoErr	;Return no error.*** Subroutines common to SetLETextByID and GetLETextByID** lineEditSetup -- set up the stack frame, get the control handle from* its ID, deref control handle into leCtlPtr, get the line edit handle* from the ctlData field, and set lineHndl and linePtr to the text.*lineEditSetup	plx	;Save return address so stack frame		;setup works.	phd	;Save directPage register.	tsc	;Make space for locals.	sec	sbc #sizeLocals	tcs	tcd	;Set directPage register.	phx	;Put return address back.	lda pstr	;Also point past p-string length	ldx pstr+2	;for c-strings.	inc a	bne @a	inx@a	sta cstr	stx cstr+2*** added 8-Aug-91 DAL, to handle window-pointer = NIL --> front window	lda <wptr+1	bne @notNIL	pha	pha	_FrontWindow	pla	sta <wptr	pla	sta <wptr+2@notNIL*** end 8-Aug-91 DAL	pha	;Get the control handle via wptr,id.	pha	pei wptr+2	pei wptr	pei lineEditID+2	pei lineEditID	_GetCtlHandleFromID	plx	stx ctlHndl	plx	stx ctlHndl+2	bcs rts1	ldy #2	;Dereference ctlHndl.	lda [ctlHndl]	sta leCtlPtr	lda [ctlHndl],y	sta leCtlPtr+2	ldy #octlData	;Get the lineEdit handle from	lda [leCtlPtr],y	;the control's data field.	sta leHndl	iny	iny	lda [leCtlPtr],y	sta leHndl+2* fall into lineEditDereflineEditDeref	ldy #2	;Dereference leHndl.	lda [leHndl]	sta lePtr	lda [leHndl],y	sta lePtr+2	ldy #oleLength	lda [lePtr],y	sta lineLength	ldy #oleLineHandle	lda [lePtr],y	sta lineHndl	iny	iny	lda [lePtr],y	sta lineHndl+2	ldy #2	;Dereference lineHndl.	lda [lineHndl]	sta linePtr	lda [lineHndl],y	sta linePtr+2	clc	;Everything worked.rts1	rts	EndP************************************************************************ $3C10 SetCtlValueByID -- added 15-Jul-92 DAL** Inputs:*   Value                 (WORD)*   Window Pointer        (LONG)*   Control ID            (LONG)***********************************************************************SetCtlValueByID	PROC EXPORT	phd	tsc	tcd@ctlID	equ 9@windPtr	equ @ctlID+4@value	equ @windPtr+4	jsr CtlGetHandle	;into XY	bcs @error	pei <@value	phx	phy	_SetCtlValue@error	tax	pld	export CtlStrip10BytesCtlStrip10Bytes	ldy #10	jml $e10184	;ToStrip	export CtlGetHandleCtlGetHandle@ctlID	equ 9@windPtr	equ @ctlID+4	pha	pha	pei <@windPtr+2	pei <@windPtr	pei <@ctlID+2	pei <@ctlID	_GetCtlHandleFromID	ply	plx	rts	ENDP************************************************************************ $3D10 GetCtlValueByID -- added 15-Jul-92 DAL** Inputs:*   Space for result      (WORD)*   Window Pointer        (LONG)*   Control ID            (LONG)***********************************************************************GetCtlValueByID	PROC EXPORT	import CtlGetHandle	phd	tsc	tcd@ctlID	equ 9@windPtr	equ @ctlID+4@result	equ @windPtr+4	stz <@result	jsr CtlGetHandle	;into XY	bcs @error	pha	phx	phy	_GetCtlValue	plx	stx <@result@error	tax	pld	export CtlStrip8BytesCtlStrip8Bytes	ldy #8	jml $e10184	;ToStrip	ENDP************************************************************************ $3E10 InvalOneCtlByID -- added 15-Jul-92 DAL** Inputs:*   Window Pointer        (LONG)*   Control ID            (LONG)***********************************************************************InvalOneCtlByID	PROC EXPORT	import CtlStrip8Bytes,CtlGetHandle	phd	tsc	tcd@ctlID	equ 9@windPtr	equ @ctlID+4	jsr CtlGetHandle	bcs @error@handle	equ @ctlID	;re-use our direct page space@ptr	equ @windPtr	stx <@handle+2	sty <@handle	ldy #4	lda [<@handle],y	pha	ora #$8000	sta [<@handle],y	dey	dey	lda [<@handle],y	sta <@ptr+2	lda [<@handle]	sta <@ptr	pha	pha	_GetPort	ldy #6	;offset to ctlOwner+2	lda [<@ptr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<@ptr],y	pha	_SetPort	ldx <@ptr+2	lda <@ptr	adc #8	bcc @1	inx@1	phx	pha	_InvalRect	_SetPort	ldy #4	pla	sta [<@handle],y	;unlock handle	lda #0	;no error@error	tax	pld	bra CtlStrip8Bytes	ENDP************************************************************************ $3F10 HiliteCtlByID -- added 15-Jul-92 DAL** Inputs:*   Hilite                (WORD)*   Window Pointer        (LONG)*   Control ID            (LONG)***********************************************************************HiliteCtlByID	PROC EXPORT	import CtlStrip10Bytes,CtlGetHandle	phd	tsc	tcd@ctlID	equ 9@windPtr	equ @ctlID+4@Hilite	equ @windPtr+4	jsr CtlGetHandle	;into XY	bcs @error	pei <@Hilite	phx	phy	_HiliteControl@error	tax	pld	brl CtlStrip10Bytes	ENDP;====================================================================;;	Set2Draw;;          	Set to draw control.;;   IN:    Ctlhand = handle of control.;          Ctlptr =	pointer to control.;;====================================================================set2draw	PROC EXPORT	pei <work+2	Save.	pei <work;	jsr to_wport	Switch to window's port.;;; --- Get window's vis RECT to not draw controls that aren't visible -------;	pha	Space for result.	pha	_GetVisHandle	Get handle of window's visRgn.	pla	sta <work	pla	sta <work+2;	ldy #2	Dereference handle,	lda [<work],y	tay	lda [<work]	clc	adc #2	and add offset to bounds RECT.	bcc store1	inystore1	sta <work	sty <work+2;	ldy #x2	Clone visRgn's bounds RECT.	ldx #visRect+x2lop1	lda [<work],y	phy	txy	sta [<data],y	ply	dex	dex	dey	dey	bpl lop1;	pla	Restore.	sta <work	pla	sta <work+2		rts		ENDP;====================================================================;;          DrawWholeCtl;;====================================================================drawWholeCtl	PROC	stz <param	Draw entire control.	;---------------------------------------------------------------;;   IN:    param = 0 to draw entire control, or part code to draw.;;---------------------------------------------------------------	ENTRY drawCtldrawCtl		;       	stz <param+2;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).;	ldy #CtlFlag	Is control visible?	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #Ctl_INVIS	bne exit;	jsr CMsetrect	Put enclosing RECT into 'rect'.;	ldy #CtlProc+2	Special case simple	buttons.	lda [<ctlptr],y	and #$7FFF	Mask off high bit just in case this is a super control	dey	dey	ora [<ctlptr],y	bne ok1;	ldy #CtlFlag	lda [<ctlptr],y	and #SB_BOLD	beq ok1;	jsr expandButt	Expand the enclosing RECT.;ok1	lda <rect+y1	bmi skip1	ldy #visRect+y2	cmp [<data],y	bcs exit;skip1	lda <rect+x1	bmi skip2	ldy #visRect+x2	cmp [<data],y	bcs exit;skip2	ldy #visRect+y1	lda [<data],y	bmi ok2	lda <rect+y2	bmi exit	ldy #visRect+y1	cmp [<data],y	bcc exit;	ldy #visRect+x1	lda [<data],y	bmi ok2	lda <rect+x2	bmi exit	ldy #visRect+x1	cmp [<data],y	bcs ok2exit	rts;ok2	jsr set2drawCtl	Setup to draw the control.;	ldx #drawCntl	Draw task number.	brl CMDispatch2	Call definition procedure.		ENDP;====================================================================;;	Set2DrawCtl;;          	Setup to draw a control.;;   IN:    <ctlHand	= handle of control.;;  OUT:    <param =	0 to draw entire control, state = 0.;	part code to draw just that part of the	control.;;           state =	0 to draw part in 'param' as unhighlighted.;	2 to draw part in 'param' as highlighted.;;           active = $0000 if control is active.;	 $FFFF if control is inactive, param = 0.;;; Change History;; 06 Oct 88	Steven Glass;; The active flag used by built in defProcs is in the global data; area rather passed to the defproc.  This made it hard for; custom defProcs to do the right thing.  So we also put; the flag in the hi-word of the param sent with the draw message;;====================================================================set2drawCtl	PROC EXPORT	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).;	lda #0	ldy #active	Set active flag.	sta [<data],y	ldy #state	Set unhighlighted flag.	sta [<data],y	stz <param+2	Zero this to indicate that control not inactive;	jsr get_wptr	Get control's window pointer.	ldy #owFrame	lda [<windptr],y	and #F_HIGHLT+F_Ctl_TIE Is owner window	active?	beq inactive	If not, control can't be either.;	ldy #CtlHilite	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #$00FF	cmp #255	Active?	bne skip;inactive	ldy #active	Set inactive flag.	lda #$FFFF	sta [<data],y	sta <param+2	stz <param	Draw entire control	as inactive.	bra ready;Skip	tax	Hilite a part?	beq ready;	sta <param	Store part to hilite in 'param'.;	ldy #state	Set highlight flag.	lda #2	sta [<data],y;;; --- Do some more,	common setups ----------------------;Ready	jsr CMsetrect	Put enclosing RECT into 'rect'.;;; No longer do we setup the ref to color table!    SEG  19 Feb 89;	jsr setupColor;	_PenNormal	; so call pen normal directly;; End 19 Feb change.;	bra setvertpen	Set pen size to vert_pen,1.; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = =;          Set pen size to:;                width = vert_pen.;                height = 1.; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = =;	ENTRY SetVertPensetvertpen	proc export;	jsr pushVvert_pen	pea 1	_SetPenSize		rts; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = =;          Draw a line from the current;          pen position, to the given point.;;   IN:  y = y coordinate.;        x = x coordinate.;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = =;	ENTRY drawtodrawto	proc export;	phx	phy	_LineTo		rts; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = =;        Indent 'rect'.;;   IN:  a = number	of lines to indent.;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = =	ENTRY indentindent		;       ;	pha;	clc	adc <rect+y1	sta <rect+y1;	lda 1,s	clc	adc <rect+x1	sta <rect+x1;	lda <rect+y2	sec	sbc 1,s	sta <rect+y2;	lda <rect+x2	sec	sbc 1,s	sta <rect+x2;	pla		rts;	ENDP;====================================================================;;	GrowSize;;          	Return the size of a standard grow box.;;   IN:    None.;;  OUT:    LONG - low order = height.;                 high-order = width.;;====================================================================GrowSize	PROCgrow_h	equ inputsgrow_w	equ grow_h+2;;	cmp #0	Special Kludge for people who	bne GoOn	open windows before	initing ctlmgr.	cpy #0	Instead of dying, we just return.	bne GoOn	(Window mgr calls this even when	lda #$1002	window has no controls.)	sec		rtlGoOn		; ;	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setups.;	ldx #GROW_ICON	jsr get_csize	Get height and width of grow icon.;	ldy #rect2+y2	Icon height,	lda [<data],y	clc	adc #4	plus leading.	sta <grow_h	equals box's height.;	ldy #rect2+x2	Icon width,	lda [<data],y	clc	adc #8	plus leading,	sta <grow_w	equals box's width.;exit	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop0bytes		ENDP;;            APPEND	CTRACK.ASM;;====================================================================;;	TrackControl;;        	Track mouse in a control.;;   IN:    PUSH:WORD - x starting position, in global.;          PUSH:WORD - y starting position, in global.;          PUSH:LONG - address of action routine.;          PUSH:LONG - handle of control.;          Current port is control's window port.;;  OUT:    WORD - part code selected, or zero if none.;;; Change History;; 21 Nov 88	Steven Glass;; Changed the way the ctlDrag message is used when control has; part code > $80.  If the control is a super control, the high; word of the result from defProc call is the part code to return; to caller.  This allows us to return no part code if the ; user pulls his mouse out of the control before releasing; the button.;;====================================================================TrackControl	PROCmatch	equ work	Place to store part	I'll be watching.control	equ inputsaction	equ control+4starty	equ action+4startx	equ starty+2RetCode	equ startx+2	Place to store current part;	                  (either what's in 'match' or zero).;;	jsr CMStartup	Do setup for tool call.;	jsr getCtlHand	Get passed control handle.	bcc ok1	Null handle passed?	brl CMpop12bytes;ok1	stz <RetCode	Start with no part found.	stz <match;	jsr to_wport	Save port and switch to window's.	jsr pushPort	Save the current port.;;; --- Convert starting point to local -----------------------;	ldx <startx	lda <starty	jsr to_local;	jsr testpart	We have to start on	a part.	sta <match	Save starting part.	bne ck_indic	Did we start on a part?	brl exit	If not, I'm done.;ck_indic	tax	Save part code in x.	and #$0080	Is the part an indicator?	bne indicator	If yes, different tracking method.;;; --- Track LOOP -----------------------------------------------------;; ------ Find out what part the cursor is currently over -------------;track_loop	jsr ckhit	Check hit on part, save state, draw.;	lda <RetCode	Is the part currently selected?	beq skip1;	sta <param	Pass part code.	stz <param+2	jsr do_action	Call action procedure.;skip1	jsr getratpos	Get current mouse position.;	jsr ckbutton2	Check if button has	been released.	bcs track_loop	Continue to track if still down.;	sta <yrat	stx <xrat	jsr ckhit	Perform check at position of up event.;;; --- Selection made, unhighlight part if needed -----------;	lda <RetCode	Not needed if zero.	beq exit1	Tell action proc it's out of part.;	lda #0	Unhilite flag.	jsr setstate	Unhilite the control part.	bra exit	All done, exit TrackControl.;;;;;;;     One-Way Code,	we pass through here only once per event.;; --- Track indicator ----------------------------------------------;; ------ Ask control to drag its indicator -------------------------;indicator	stx <RetCode	Return part code.;	ldy #0	(High word of LONG parameter.)	txa	Pass part code to drag routine.	ldx #dragCntl	jsr CMDispatch	pha	Save low word of return	cmp #0	If not handled, treat as not super	beq @NotSuper	ldy #ctlProc+2	See if this is a super control	lda [<ctlPtr],y	bpl @NotSuper	No, not a super control	stx <RetCode	Yes, make this the part code@NotSuper	pla	Now, check to see if we do default dragging?	bne exit;;; --------- Perform	default indicator drag -------------------------;	jsr pushlimit_blk	pla	Pass pointer to parameter block	ply	ldx #thumbCntl	Ask defProc to compute parameters.	jsr CMDispatch	Call control.	tax	Execute default setup?	bne call_drag;	jsr setup_drag	Perform default setup for dragging.;;; --- Call DragRect	------------------------------------------------;call_drag	jsr get_dragrect	Compute drag RECT.;	pha	Space for return deltas.	pha	lda #0	Address of action procedure, none.	pha	pha	jsr pushVdrag_patt	Pass to drag outline pattern.	pei <xrat	Pass starting point.	pei <yrat	jsr pushdrag_rect	Pass pointer to RECT to drag.	jsr pushbound_rect	Pass pointer to bounds RECT.	jsr pushslop_rect	Pass pointer to slop RECT.	jsr pushVaxis_param	Pass movement axis parameter.	_DragRect	pla	Get Y delta.	sta <param	pla	Get X delta.	sta <param+2	ora <param	Was there any change?	beq exit	If not, I'm done.;;; --- Reposition indicator -----------------------------------------;	ldx #posCntl	Ask defProc to compute new value,	jsr CMDispatch2	and redraw control.	tax	Perform default reposition?	bne exit1;	jsr reposition	Perform default reposition.;exit1	jsr do_action	Call action routine	about change.;exit	jsr popPort	Restore the current	port.;exit2	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop12bytes;;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = =;          Check hit on part.;100= = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = =;ckhit		; ;	lda <yrat	Find part under cursor.	ldx <xrat	jsr testpart	beq ck_hilite	Over a part?;	cmp <match	Has to be the same as the starting part.	beq ck_hilite	lda #0	Force it to 'out of part'.;;; ------ Highlight/Unhighlight the part	as needed --------------------;ck_hilite	cmp <RetCode	As state of part changed?	beq exit100;	sta <RetCode	Save new state.	brl setstate	Draw the part in its new state.;exit100	rts;;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = =;          Push a pointer to inside a record.;110= = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = =;;   IN:    Ctlptr =	pointer to record.;          a = offset into the record.;;  OUT:    pointer on stack.;;	export pushrecordpushrecord	proc export;	ply	Get return address.;	ldx <Ctlptr+2	clc	adc <Ctlptr	bcc ok110	inxok110	phx	pha;	phy	Return address back.	rts;;;====================================================================;          Call action procedure.;;          action =	value passed to TrackControl.;          CtlAction = value in control's record.;          autoTrack = control's definition procedure's action command.;;          If action = 0 then quit, perform no action.;          If action = -1 then;          {;                If	CtlAction = 0 then quit, perform no action.;                If	CtlAction = -1 then;	  Call autoTrack in	the control's definition procedure.;                Else;	  Call CtlAction.;          };          Else;                Call action.;;120=================================================================do_action	proc export	;made into proc, 8-Dec-91 for TS3*** duplicate equates, 8-Dec-91 DALcontrol	equ inputsaction	equ control+4starty	equ action+4startx	equ starty+2RetCode	equ startx+2	Place to store current part;	                  (either what's in 'match' or zero).*** end 8-Dec-91	lda <action	Perform no action?	ora <action+2	beq exit120;	lda <action+2	bpl use_action	If negative, call defProc for autoTrack.;; ------------ Check CtlAction for path	to take ---------------------;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #CtlAction	lda [<Ctlptr],y	iny	iny	ora [<Ctlptr],y	Is CtlAction zero?	beq exit120	If yes, perform no action.;	lda [<Ctlptr],y	bpl use_Ctl;; -----------------	Call defProc's action routine -------------------;	ldx #autoTrack	Part code already in param.	brl CMDispatch2;;; -----------------	Call CtlAction ---------------------------------;use_Ctl	dey	lda [<Ctlptr],y	tax	ldy #CtlAction	lda [<Ctlptr],y	bra makecall;;; -----------------	Use action routine passed to TrackControl --------;use_action	ldx <action+1	lda <action;;; --------- Call action routine that was passed to _TrackControl -----;makecall	tay	Pass address in X and Y.;;	pei <ctlhand+2	Save control's handle.	pei <ctlhand	phd	Save my zero page.;;	pha	Space for dummy return value,;	                  to make some apps run.	pei <RetCode	Pass part code.	pei <Ctlhand+2	Pass handle of control.	pei <Ctlhand;	lda <saveDirect	Restore caller's direct page.	tcd;	tya	Pass low byte in A.	jsl long_call;	pla	Get dummy return value (not used).;	pld	Restore my zero page.	pla	Restore control's handle.	sta <ctlhand	pla	sta <ctlhand+2	brl dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).;exit120	rts; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = = = =;        Find part at given point;;   IN:  a = y coordinate.;        x = x coordinate.;        <ctlHand =	handle of control.;;  OUT:    Equal flag TRUE if no part found.;          Else;                a = part code found at	given point, or zero if none found.;;130= = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = = = =	ENTRY testparttestpart		;       	sta <param	Pass y point.	stx <param+2	Pass x point.	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #CtlFlag	Control has to be active and visible.	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #Ctl_INVIS	bne noPart130	Visible?;	iny	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #$00FF	cmp #C_HILITE	Active?	bne ok130noPart130	lda #0	No part	rts;ok130	ldy #CtlRect	Is point in enclosing RECT?	jsr check_pt	beq exit130	Don't check part if not in control.;	ldx #testCntl	Call defProc to test for part.	jsr CMDispatch2;	tay	Set return flag.	exit130	rts; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = = = =;;        Set state of control.;;   IN:    a = part	code to highlight, or zero to unhighlight last highlighted.;;150= = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = = = =	ENTRY setstatesetstate		;       	pha	Pass part code to highlight.	pei <Ctlhand+2	Pass handle of control.	pei <Ctlhand	_HiliteControl	Change control highlight and draw.;	brl dereference;;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = = = =;;        Check if button is stil down.;;  OUT:  Carry set if button still down.;        Carry clear if button has been	released, a=y pos, x=x pos.;;; Change History;; 09 Apr 89	Steven Glass & James P. Mensch;; Simplified check for mouse coming up when we think it ; should be down.  Prevents leaving a mouse up in queue.;;160= = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = = = =	ENTRY ckbutton2ckbutton2		;       	pha	pea 4	Looking only for button up.	jsr pushmyevent	Pass pointer to event record.	_GetNextEvent	pla	bne getevent;;; --- Button has not come up yet, but double check ----------------------;	ldy #MyEvent+modif	Read modifiers from event	lda [<Data],y	and #Btn0State	Look only at button 0 state (Sense is weird)	bne GetEvent	Button is up, treat like got event.	sec	Return 'still down flag'.	rts;;; --- Button up event, use position of event -------------------------------;getevent	jsr pushmyeventpos	_GlobalToLocal;exit160	ldy #myevent+where+x1 Return position of button up.	lda [<data],y	tax	dey	dey	lda [<data],y	clc	Button up flag.		rts; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = = = =;;        Get current mouse position.;;  OUT:  yrat = mouse y position.;        xrat = mouse x position.;;170= = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = = = =	ENTRY getratposgetratpos		;       	lda #yrat;	ENTRY getratpos2getratpos2		;       	jsr pushzpage	_GetMouse		rts;	ENDP;====================================================================;          Long call.;;   IN:    x = middle WORD (bits 8-23) of address of destination routine.;          a = low WORD of address of destination routine.;;  OUT:    Calling this routine is the same as:;;                jsl   (ax);;          where the low byte in 'a' is	the low byte of the	destination;          address,	and x = the next 2 bytes of the destination address.;;====================================================================long_call	PROC EXPORT	phx	High and middle byte on stack	phb	extra byte on stack	dec a	low and middle := xxx -1	sta 1,s	overstore on stack	rtl	hello;;  When the routine	called returns, it;  will return to the routine that called 'longCall', not here.;	ENDP;====================================================================;;          Move a control to a new position.;;   IN:    PUSH:WORD - new x origin of control.;          PUSH:WORD - new y origin of control.;          PUSH:LONG - handle of control to move.;;  OUT:    Nothing.;;====================================================================MoveControl	PROCCtlHandle	equ inputsnew_y	equ CtlHandle+4new_x	equ new_y+2;;	jsr CMStartup	Do setup for tool call.;	jsr getCtlHand	Get passed control handle.	bcs exit	Null handle passed?;	ldy #4	Lock the control.	lda [<ctlHand],y	ora #$8000	sta [<ctlHand],y;;; --- Erase the control if visible ---------------------------;	ldy #CtlFlag	Is control visible?	lda [<Ctlptr],y	and #Ctl_INVIS	pha	Save starting state.	bne skip1;	pei <Ctlhand+2	pei <Ctlhand	_HideControl	Erase the control.;;; --- Move the control --------------------------------------;skip1	lda #CtlRect	Pass pointer to enclosing RECT.	jsr pushrecord	lda <new_x	ldy #CtlRect+x1	sec	sbc [<Ctlptr],y	sta <new_x	Save delta x.	pha	lda <new_y	dey	dey	sec	sbc [<Ctlptr],y	sta <new_y	Save delta y.	pha	_OffsetRect	Move the enclosing RECT.;	ldy <new_x	Pass X delta.	lda <new_y	Pass Y delta.	ldx #moveCntl	Tell defProc that the control has moved.	jsr CMDispatch	and redraw control.;;; --- Draw the control at its new position if it was visible -----------;	pla	Was the control visible?	bne exit;	pei <Ctlhand+2	pei <Ctlhand	_ShowControl;exit	ldy #4	Unlock control.	lda [<ctlHand],y	and #$7FFF	sta [<ctlHand],y;	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop8bytes		ENDP;====================================================================;;          Find a control at a given point.;;   IN:    PUSH:LONG - address of where	to store handle of found control.;          PUSH:WORD - x point to check.;          PUSH:WORD - y point to check.;          PUSH:LONG - pointer to window.;          Current port is window's port.;;  OUT:    WORD - part code found at given point, zero if none found.;;====================================================================FindControl	PROCwindow	equ inputsypoint	equ window+4xpoint	equ ypoint+2storehand	equ xpoint+2RetPart	equ storehand+4;;	jsr CMStartup	Do setup for tool call.;	stz <RetPart	Start with no part found.;	jsr getWindPtr	Get given window pointer.	bcs exit2	Any errors?;;; --- Switch to control's window port --------------------------;	jsr to_wport;;; --- Convert given	point to local ------------------------------;	ldx <xpoint	lda <ypoint	jsr to_local	sta <ypoint	stx <xpoint;;; --- Check all controls in list -----------------------------;	stz <ctlhand	Start with last control in list.	stz <ctlhand+2	jsr findPrivCtl	ctlhand = last control in list.;	                  ctlptr = (ctlhand);lop1	ldx <xpoint	lda <ypoint	jsr testpart	Ask control's DefProc to find part.	sta <RetPart	tax	bne exit	Found a part?	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).;next1	jsr findPrivCtl	ctlhand, ctlptr = previous control.	bcc lop1	At top of list?;;;; --- Return to caller ----------------------------------;exit	lda <Ctlhand	Return pointer to control.	sta [<storehand]	ldy #2	lda <Ctlhand+2	sta [<storehand],y;exit2	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop12bytes;;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = =;          Find previsous control in list.; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = =;;   IN:    windPtr = pointer to window that has control list.;          ctlhand = current control, zero for last in list.;;  OUT:    Carry clear if good control found.;          ctlhand = control previous to given control in control list.;          ctlptr =	(ctlhand);findPrivCtl		; ;	lda <ctlhand	Save control to match.	sta <work	lda <ctlhand+2	sta <work+2;	jsr getFirstCtl	ctlhand = first control in window's list.;	                  ctlptr = (ctlhand).;	lda <ctlhand	Check if at top of list.	cmp <work	bne lop100	lda <ctlHand+2	cmp <work+2	beq exit100	Carry set, at top of list.;lop100	lda [<ctlptr]	Handle of next control.	cmp <work	Is the next control	the given handle?	bne next100	ldy #CtlNext+2	lda [<ctlptr],y	cmp <work+2	clc	beq exit100	If yes, then previous control found.;next100	jsr next_ctl	Check next control in list.	bne lop100	Any more controls in list?	sec	!!!Should never happen!!!!;exit100	rts;	ENDP;;;====================================================================;;          Convert a point to;          local coordinates.;;   IN:    a = y point.;          x = x point.;;  OUT:    a = y point in local.;          x = x point in local.;;====================================================================to_local	PROC	sta <yrat	Save point.	stx <xrat;	jsr pushyrat	Pass pointer to point.	_GlobalToLocal;	lda <yrat	Return converted point.	ldx <xrat		rts	ENDP;====================================================================;;        Find a control part at a given	point.;;   IN:  PUSH:WORD - x point, in local coordinates, to check.;        PUSH:WORD - y point, in local coordinates, to check.;        PUSH:LONG - pointer to control	(control list).;;  OUT:  WORD - part code found at given point, zero if none found.;; Parts are searched from bottom of list to top, as they appear on screen.;;====================================================================TestControl	PROCcontrol	equ inputsypoint	equ control+4xpoint	equ ypoint+2RetPart	equ xpoint+2;;	jsr CMStartup	Do setup for tool call.;	jsr getCtlHand	Get passed control handle.	bcs exit	Null handle passed?;	ldx <xpoint	Pass point to check.	lda <ypoint	jsr testpart	sta <RetPart;exit	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop8bytes		ENDP;====================================================================;;          Drag a control.;;   IN:    PUSH:WORD - starting x coordinate, in local.;          PUSH:WORD - starting y coordinate, in local.;          PUSH:LONG - pointer to RECT that is bounds of movement, in local.;          PUSH:LONG - pointer to RECT that is cusor limit,	in local.;          PUSH:WORD - movement constraint.;          PUSH:LONG - handle of control.;;  OUT:    None.;;====================================================================DragControl	PROCtheControl	equ inputsaxis	equ theControl+4slop	equ axis+2limit	equ slop+4starty	equ limit+4startx	equ starty+2;;	jsr CMStartup	Do setup for tool call.;	jsr getCtlHand	Get passed control handle.	bcs exit	Null handle passed?;;; --- Ask control to drag control ---------------------------;	ldy #0	Drag whole control flag.	tya	ldx #dragCntl	jsr CMDispatch	tax	Do default dragging?	bne exit;;; ------ Perform default drag --------------------------------;	stz <param	Drag whole control flag.	jsr get_dragrect	Ask control to compute drag RECT.;;; --------- Call drag RECT -----------------------------------------;	pha	Space for result.	pha	lda #0	No action routine.	pha	pha	ldy #$00F0	Solid drag pattern.	jsr set_patt	phx	phy	pei <startx	Pass starting point.	pei <starty	jsr pushdrag_rect	Pass address of RECT to drag.	pei <limit+2	pei <limit	pei <slop+2	pei <slop	pei <axis	_DragRect	pla	Get delta y.	sta <work	pla	Get delta x.	sta <work+2	ora <work	Was there any movement?	beq exit;;; --- Now move control to it's new spot ---------------------;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).;	ldy #CtlRect+x1	Compute new origin and pass it.	lda [<Ctlptr],y	clc	adc <work+2	pha	dey	dey	lda [<Ctlptr],y	clc	adc <work	pha	pei <Ctlhand+2	Pass handle of control.	pei <Ctlhand	_MoveControl;;exit	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop18bytes		ENDP;====================================================================;;          Ask control to compute drag RECT.;;   IN:    param = zero for whole control, nonzero for part.;;  OUT:    drag_rect = RECT to drag, in	local coordinates.;;====================================================================get_dragrect	PROC	jsr pushdrag_rect;	lda <param	Whole control?	beq ok1;	lda 3,s	Get high word of address,	ora #$8000	Set 'just the part'	flag.	sta 3,s;ok1	pla	Get pointer to drag_rect with high bit	ply	set correctly.;;;  a = low word of where to store RECT.;  y = high word of	where to store RECT,;	              high bit clear for whole control,;	              high bit set for control part.;	ldx #calcCRect	jsr CMDispatch	Call control.	tax	bne exit	Default?;;; ------ Use default drag RECT -------------------------------------;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #CtlRect	Whole control.	lda <param+2	Indicator or whole control?	bpl ok2	ldy #Thumb	Just the indicator.ok2	ldx #drag_rectlop1	lda [<Ctlptr],y	phy	txy	sta [<data],y	ply	iny	iny	inx	inx	cpx #drag_rect+8	bne lop1;exit	rts	ENDP;====================================================================;;	CallDefProc;;        	Calls a controls defproc with the specified inputs.;;   IN:  PUSH:LONG - Space for result;        PUSH:LONG - Control Handle;        PUSH:WORD - Message to Send;        PUSH:LONG - Value for Param;;  OUT:  PULL:LONG-  Result from DefProc.;; Change History;; 03 Oct 88	Steven Glass;; New today;; 06 Oct 88	Steven Glass;; Cannot use GetCtlHandle because it expects the handle ; at Inputs on zero page.;;====================================================================CallDefProc	PROCTheParam	equ inputsTheMessage	equ TheParam+4TheControl	equ TheMessage+2TheResult	equ TheControl+4;;	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setup.;	lda TheControl,s	sta ctlHand	lda TheControl+2,s	sta ctlHand+2	jsr Dereference;	jsr set2draw	Setup to draw standard controls.	jsr pushPort	Save the current port.	jsr set2drawCtl	Setup to draw the control.;	lda <TheParam	Pass new view and data sizes.	ldy <TheParam+2	ldx <TheMessage	Task number.	jsr CMDispatch	sta TheResult	stx TheResult+2	jsr popPort	Restore the current	port.;exit	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop10bytes		ENDP	title 'Param Text Routines';====================================================================;;	SetCtlParamPtr;;   Puts the indicated pointer into the global data area.;;   IN:  PUSH:LONG - Pointer to sub array;;  OUT:  none.;; Change History;; 21 Oct 88	Steven Glass;; New today;;====================================================================SetCtlParamPtr	PROCThePtr	equ inputs	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setup.	lda ThePtr	ldy #ParamTextPtr	sta [<data],y	iny	iny	lda ThePtr+2	sta [<data],y	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop4bytes		ENDP;====================================================================;;	GetCtlParamPtr;;   Returns the paramtext pointer from the global data area.;;   IN:  PUSH:LONG - space for pointer;;  OUT:  PULL:LONG - pointer to current substitution array.;; Change History;; 21 Oct 88	Steven Glass;; New today;;====================================================================GetCtlParamPtr	PROCThePtr	equ inputs	jsr CMStartup	Do tool function setup.	ldy #ParamTextPtr	lda [<data],y	sta ThePtr	iny	iny	lda [<data],y	sta ThePtr+2	ldy #0	No error flag.	brl CMpop0bytes		ENDP	title 'Dispatching Code';====================================================================;;          CMDispatch	task.;;   IN:    x = task.;          Ctlptr =	pointer to control.;          a = param.;          y = param+2.;;  OUT:    a = low word of returned value.;          x = high	word of returned value.;;; Change History;; 05 Oct 88	Steven Glass;; Major changes to support super controls.;; 11 Oct 88	Steven Glass;; Make this routine patchable.;; 24 Oct 88	Steven Glass;; Added calls to TextEdit and Menu Manager.  Simplified code for; new builtin procs.;; 10 Feb 89	Steven Glass;; Changed code that calls load resource so that it will load ; not use an id with the high bit set (not valid for the resource; manager.);;====================================================================CMDispatch	PROC EXPORT	sta <param	sty <param+2;;	ENTRY CMDispatch2CMDispatch2		;       ;;   IN:    param = additional parameter.;	phx	Save.	ldx #oCMDispatcher	jml ToolboxPatcher	EXPORT RealCMDispatcherRealCMDispatcher	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).;-----------------------------------------------------------;; See if this is a super control.  If it is, there can ; be more work to do.  Otherwise, go the old way.;	ldy #NewCtlRecord.CtlProc+2	lda [ctlPtr],y	bpl DoOldWay;-----------------------------------------------------------;; It is a super control.  Must see if we have pointer to; defproc or an ID.;	clc		Assume that it is a pointer	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlMoreFlags	Now, look and see what it really is	lda [ctlPtr],y	and #FctlProcRefNotPtr	beq ItsAPtr	sec		its a resourceItsAPtr	ldy #NewCtlRecord.CtlProc+2	Get reference into a & y	lda [ctlPtr],y		with message in x.	tax	dey	dey	lda [ctlPtr],y	txy	plx	bcs CallByThisID	bra CallByThisPtrDoOldWay	plx	Restore.	ldy #CtlProc	Is this a custom control?	lda [<Ctlptr],y	bne do_custom	iny	lda [<Ctlptr],y	bne do_custom;;; --- Call a standard control definition procedure --------------;	iny	lda [<Ctlptr],y	Get control number.;	EXPORT standardDispatchstandardDispatch		;       ;	phx	Save task number.	and #$7FFF	; Clear off super control bit.	xba	Get standard defProc number into low byte.	tax	Put index into X.	pla	Put task number into A.	jmp (my_procs,x)	Get address of standard procedure.;my_procs	DC.W simp_proc	Simple button procedure.	DC.W check_proc	Check box procedure.	DC.W radio_proc	Radio button procedure.	DC.W scroll_proc	Scroll bar procedure.	DC.W grow_proc	Grow box procedure.;;; --- Call a custom	control definition procedure ----------------;do_custom	phx	Save task number.	ldy #CtlProc+1	Get address of defProc.	lda [<Ctlptr],y	tax	dey	lda [<Ctlptr],y	ply	Get task number.;;;   IN:    y = task	number.;          a = bytes 0 and 1 of defProc	address.;          x = bytes 1 and 2 of defProc	address.;          param = additional parameters.;	ENTRY customDispatchcustomDispatch		;       ;	pei <Ctlhand+2	Save current handle	of control.	pei <Ctlhand;	pha	Space for return value.	pha;	phy	Pass task number.;	pei <param+2	Pass additional parameters.	pei <param;	pei <Ctlhand+2	Pass control's handle.	pei <Ctlhand;	jsl long_call	Call custom defProc.	pla	Get return values.	plx;	ply	Restore Ctlhand.	sty <Ctlhand	ply	sty <Ctlhand+2;	rts;-----------------------------------------------------------;; CallByThisPtr;;   Inputs:;      a-reg  low word of procPtr;      y-reg  high word of procPtr;      x-reg  message to send;	Export CallByThisPtrCallByThisPtr	phx	Put message on stack	phy	put high word on stack	pha	put low word on stack	lda 2,s	get middle and high bytes into x	tax	pla	get low back into a	ply	ignore high word	ply	message into y	bra CustomDispatch;-----------------------------------------------------------;; CallByThisID;;   Inputs:;      a-reg  low word of ID;      y-reg  high word of ID;      x-reg  message to send;; this routine has to see if the ID is one of our special; ID's or if it is a normal resource ID.;; The special IDs have the low three bytes set to zero.; These include the original defprocs as well as ; new built in defprocs and some new standard non ; build in defprocs.;	Export CallByThisIDCallByThisID	phx	Save message	phy	save ID	pha	lda 1,s	Is low word 0	bne NotSpecial	no	lda 2,s	Is middle word 0	bne NotSpecial	no	lda 4,s	Yes	and #$007F	Clear super ctl bit	cmp #LastSpecial+1	Is it in range?	bcs NotSpecial	no	asl a	Use as index into table	tax	jmp (WhereTable,x)	WhereTable	dc.w OldBuiltIn	simpleButtonControl	equ $80000000	dc.w DoStatText	statTextControl	equ $81000000	dc.w OldBuiltIn	checkControl	equ $82000000	dc.w ItsALineEdit	LineEditControl	equ $83000000	dc.w OldBuiltIn	radioControl	equ $84000000	dc.w ItsATextEdit	TextEditControl	equ $85000000	dc.w OldBuiltIn	scrollBarControl	equ $86000000	dc.w ItsAPopUp	popUpControl	equ $87000000	dc.w OldBuiltIn	growControl	equ $88000000	dc.w ItsAList	listControl	equ $89000000	dc.w NotSpecial	not used???	dc.w NotSpecial	iconButtonControl	equ $8B000000	dc.w NotSpecial     not used 	dc.w DoPicture	pictureControl	equ $8D000000LastSpecial	equ (*-WhereTable)>>1;-----------------------------------------------------------;; NotSpecial;; Inputs: (on stack);    Msg : WORD;    ID : LONG;; We get here if we have to load the defProc's code resource;NotSpecial	plx		Get ID into a & X	pla	and #$7FFF		Ignore super control bit	ply		Get message into y	pha		Put four bytes on stack for use below	pha	PushWord #rCtlDefProc	Push rType and ID for	pha		later	phx	phy		Save Message	pha		Space for result	pha	PushWord #rCtlDefProc	pha	phx	jsr LoadCodeResource	lda 2,s		put middle word into x	tax	pla		low word into a	ply		ignore high word	ply		message	jsr CustomDispatch	sta 7,s		put result back into	txa		space on stack reserved above	sta 9,s	jsr ReleaseResource		(inputs on stack above)	pla		return result in a & x	plx	rts;-----------------------------------------------------------;; We get here if the Proc is an old style build in; defproc.  We set up the reg and xfer to Standard Dispatch;OldBuiltIn	pla		low word of ProcRef	pla		high word of ProcRef	plx		Message	brl StandardDispatch;-----------------------------------------------------------;; We get here if the control is a static text control.;;   Stack is     Msg;                id high;                id low;; So we setup the regs and branch to CustomDispatch.;DoStatText	ldx #>StatTextProc	lda #<StatTextProc	bra FinishUp;-----------------------------------------------------------;; We get here if the control is a picture control;;   Stack is     Msg;                id high;                id low;; So we setup the regs and branch to CustomDispatch.;DoPicture	ldx #>PicProc	lda #<PicProcFinishUp	ply	ply	ply	brl CustomDispatch;-----------------------------------------------------------;; ItsAList;; We get here if the Proc supposed to be in the list manager.;; Inputs: (on stack);    Msg : WORD;    ID : LONG;;ItsAList	pha	pha	_GetListDefProc	bra JoinExternal;-----------------------------------------------------------;; ItsAPopUp;; We get here if the Proc supposed to be in the menu manager.;; Inputs: (on stack);    Msg : WORD;    ID : LONG;;ItsAPopUp	pha	pha	_GetPopUpDefProc	bra JoinExternal;-----------------------------------------------------------;; ItsATextEdit;; We get here if the Proc supposed to be in text edit.;; Inputs: (on stack);    Msg : WORD;    ID : LONG;;ItsATextEdit	pha	pha	_TEGetDefProc	bra JoinExternal;-----------------------------------------------------------;; ItsALineEdit;; We get here if the Proc supposed to be the line edit;; Inputs: (on stack);    Msg : WORD;    ID : LONG;;ItsALineEdit	pha	pha	_GetLEDefProcJoinExternal	lda 2,s	tax	lda 1,s	ply	ply		ply		low word of ProcRef	ply		high word of ProcRef	ply		Message	brl CustomDispatch	ENDP***********************************************************************CMLoadResource	PROC EXPORT** This is an external entry to the LoadResource call below.** Inputs:*	HandleSpace : LONG*	Type        : WORD*	ID          : ID** Outputs:*	ResourceHandle************************************************************************	DefineStackOrigD	wordRTL1	block 3RTL2	block 3TheID	longTheType	wordTheHandle	word	import GetAndSetPrefs	phd	tsc	tcd*** added 15-Sep-91 DAL	jsr GetAndSetPrefs	pha*** end 15-Sep-91	pha	pha	pei TheType	pei TheID+2	pei TheID	jsr LoadResource	pla	sta TheHandle	pla	sta TheHandle+2*** added 15-Sep-91 DAL	pla	jsr SetPrefsToA*** end 15-Sep-91	pld	ldx #0	ldy #6	jml ToStrip	EndP;GetAndSetPrefs	proc export;	pea $0000	;space for old prefs;	pea $0001	;pcount;	tsc;	inc a;	pea 0;	pha;	pea $200F	;GetSysPrefs;	jsl $e100b0;;	lda 3,s	;old prefs;	ora #$C000	;force vol-mount w/ no cancel;	and #$DFFF	;don't supress the dialog! (4-Dec-91 DAL);	jsr SetPrefsToA;;	pla;	pla	;A=old prefs value;	rts;;	export SetPrefsToA;SetPrefsToA	pha	;new prefs value;	pea $0001	;pcount;	tsc;	inc a;	pea 0;	pha;	pea $200C	;SetSysPrefs;	jsl $e100b0;	pla;	pla;	rts*** changed 22-Mar-93 DALGetAndSetPrefs	proc export	pha	;space for result	pea $2000	;bits to clear (don't suppress dialog)	pea $C000	;bits to set (force vol-mount, no cancel);	_DoSysPrefs	ldx #$3f03	jsl $e10000	pla	;old preferences	rts	export SetPrefsToASetPrefsToA	pha	;space for result	pea $FFFF	;bits to clear (all)	pha	;bits to set (input);	_DoSysPrefs	ldx #$3f03	jsl $e10000	pla	;discard result	rts*** end 22-Mar-93	ENDP***********************************************************************CMReleaseResource	PROC** This is an external entry to the ReleaseResource call below.** Inputs:*	Type        : WORD*	ID          : ID** Outputs:*	none************************************************************************	DefineStackOrigD	wordRTL1	block 3RTL2	block 3TheID	longTheType	word	phd	tsc	tcd	pei TheType	pei TheID+2	pei TheID	jsr ReleaseResource	pld	ldx #0	ldy #6	jml ToStrip	ENDP*****************************************************************LoadResource	PROC EXPORT** This is the single place we call LoadResource in the control* manager.  We use a single entry point to simplify error * handling.** The routine that needs LoadResource, pushes space for the result* the type and id on the stack (just like making the tool call) * and JSR's here.** Any error results in a system death.** Inputs:*	HandleSpace : LONG*	Type        : WORD*	ID          : ID** Outputs:*	ResourceHandle** External Refs:*	none** Entry Points:	EXPORT LoadCodeResource	ENTRY CMDieHorribly*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	DefineStackTheOrigD	WORDTheRTS	WORDTheID	LONGTheType	WORDTheHandle	LONG	phd	tsc	tcd	pha	pha	pei TheType	pei TheID+2	pei TheID	_LoadResource	bcs CMDieHorribly	pla	sta TheHandle	pla	sta TheHandle+2GoodJob	pld	plx	pla	pla	pla	phx	rtsLoadCodeResource	phd	tsc	tcd*** added 8-Dec-91 DAL -- force prompt, no Cancel button	jsr GetAndSetPrefs	pha*** end 8-Dec-91	pha	pha	pei TheType	pei TheID+2	pei TheID	_LoadResource	bcs CMDieHorribly	pla	; deref the handle and return the pointer	sta TheHandle	pla	sta TheHandle+2*** added 8-Dec-91 DAL -- restore system preferences	pla	jsr SetPrefsToA*** end 8-Dec-91 DAL	ldy #2	lda [TheHandle],y	tax	lda [TheHandle]	sta TheHandle	stx TheHandle+2	bra GoodJob;-----------------------------------------------------------;; The load failed, so bring us all down!;RamToTrash	equ $0002A0CMDieHorribly		sta TheHandle	PushLong #DeathMsg	PushLong #RamToTrash	lda >DeathMsg	and #$00FF	inc a	;added 20-Nov-90 DAL	pea $0000	pha	_BlockMove	lda TheID	jsr HexIt	sta >RamToTrash+IDStart-DeathMsg+4	txa	sta >RamToTrash+IDStart-DeathMsg+6	lda TheID+2	jsr HexIt	sta >RamToTrash+IDStart-DeathMsg	txa	sta >RamToTrash+IDStart-DeathMsg+2	lda TheType	jsr HexIt	sta >RamToTrash+TypeStart-DeathMsg	txa	sta >RamToTrash+TypeStart-DeathMsg+2	pei TheHandle	PushLong #RamToTrash	_SysFailMgrDeathMsg	dc.b EndMsg-StartMsgStartMsg	dc.b 'Could not load/unload resource.',13	dc.b '  Type='TypeStart	dc.b '    .',13	dc.b '  ID='IDStart	dc.b '        .',13	dc.b '  Error='EndMsgHexIt	pha	pha	pha	_HexIt	pla	plx	rts	ENDP*****************************************************************ReleaseResource	PROC EXPORT** This is the single place we call LoadResource in the control* manager.  We use a single entry point to simplify error * handling.** The routine that needs LoadResource, pushes space for the result* the type and id on the stack (just like making the tool call) * and JSR's here.** Any error results in a system death.** Inputs:*	Type        : WORD*	ID          : ID** Outputs:*	none** External Refs:	import CMDieHorribly** Entry Points:*	longa on	; mode	longi on*****************************************************************	DefineStackTheOrigD	WORDTheRTS	WORDTheID	LONGTheType	WORD	phd	tsc	tcd	PushWord #$0003	; purge level	pei TheType	pei TheID+2	pei TheID	_ReleaseResource	bcc GoodJob	jmp CMDieHorriblyGoodJob	pld	plx	pla	pla	pla	phx	rts	ENDP	TITLE 'Control Manager Utilities';====================================================================;;          Push the	contents of the current port.;;====================================================================pushPort	proc EXPORT	plx	Get return address.	tsc	Allocate space for port info.	sec	sbc #112	tcs	phx	Put return address back.;	jsr getSavePtr;	ldy #110lop1	lda [<work],y	sta [<work+4],y	dey	dey	bpl lop1;	jsr popSave		rts; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = =;          Put content of port off stack.;100= = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = =;	EXPORT popPortpopPort		;       ;	jsr getSavePtr;	ldy #110lop100	lda [<work+4],y	sta [<work],y	dey	dey	bpl lop100;	jsr popSave;	plx	Get return address.	tsc	clc	adc #112	tcs	phx	Put return address back.;	rts; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	=;          Compute pointer to part of port to save.;110= = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	=;getSavePtr	plx	pei <work+6	Save.	pei <work+4	pei <work+2	pei <work	phx;	pha	Get pointer to current port.	pha	_GetPort	pla	plx	clc	adc #$0020	bcc store110	inxstore110	sta <work	stx <work+2;	tsc	Compute pointer into stack.	clc	adc #13	sta <work+4	stz <work+6	rts;;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	=;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	=;popSave	plx	pla	Restore.	sta <work	pla	sta <work+2	pla	sta <work+4	pla	sta <work+6	phx		rts;	ENDP;====================================================================;;          Set text	color and writing mode.;;   IN:    a = normal color index into color table.;          colorptr	= pointer to color table.;          state = 0 for normal, 2 for hilited.;;====================================================================set_textmode	proc EXPORT	ldy #state	clc	adc [<data],y	tay	lda [<colorptr],y	pha	Save color.	and #$000F	Just text color.	jsr smear	Duplicate color in all 4 nibbles.	pha	Pass color of title.	_SetForeColor	Set text color.;	pla	Restore saved color.	and #$00F0	pha	lsr a	Get background color.	lsr a	lsr a	lsr a	ora 1,s	sta 1,s	xba	ora 1,s	sta 1,s	_SetBackColor;	pea 0	Copy mode.	_SetTextMode;	rts		ENDP;====================================================================;;          Smear color into all 4 nibbles.;;   IN:    a = low nibble is color.;;  OUT:    a = low nibble duplicated into all 4 nibbles.;          x = trash.;;====================================================================smear	proc EXPORT;	and #$000F	pha	asl a	asl a	asl a	asl a	ora 1,s	sta 1,s	xba	ora 1,s	plx		rts		ENDP;====================================================================;;          New icon	font.;;   IN:    a,x = handle of new icon font.;;====================================================================SetIconFont	proc EXPORT	ldy #ctl_font	Store new handle in	global variable.	sta [<data],y	iny	iny	txa	sta [<data],y;; --- Get parameters of new icon font -----------------------------------;	ldx #UP_ARROW	Get size of up arrow icon.lop110	phx	jsr get_csize	plx;	ldy #rect2+y2	Save height.	lda [<data],y	pha	lda >arrowMap-UP_ARROW,x	tay	pla	sta [<data],y	iny	iny	phy	ldy #rect2+x2	Save width.	lda [<data],y	ply	sta [<data],y;	inx	inx	cpx #RITE_ARROW+2	bne lop110;	rts		ENDP;====================================================================;;          Perform initialization for;          resolution specific values.;;====================================================================newResGuts	proc EXPORT	import ComputeScrollColor		pha	Space for result.	_GetMasterSCB	pla	ldy #GraphicsMode	and #$0080	Mask off mode bit.	sta [<data],y	Remember mode.	beq mode320;;; --- Initialize for 640 mode ------------------------------;	jsr ComputeScrollColor;;;	lda #myScrollPatt640	;added 20-Nov-90 DAL;;;	sta >scroll_color+12	;added 20-Nov-90 DAL	ldy #2	640 mode vertical line width = 2.	lda #Ctl640	640 icon font.	ldx #16	Minimum horizontal thumb size in 640.	bra enter1;;; --- Initialize for 320 mode ------------------------------;mode320	jsr ComputeScrollColor	ldy #1	320 mode vertical line width = 1.	ldx #8	Minimum horizontal thumb size in 320.	lda #Ctl320	320 icon font.;enter1	pha	tya	ldy #vert_pen	Store vertical line width to use.	sta [<data],y	pla;	ldy #fontHandle	Store font pointer in fake handle.	sta [<data],y	iny	iny	lda #Ctl320>>16	sta [<data],y;	ldy #min_thumb	Store minimum thumb	size.	txa	sta [<data],y;	jsr pushfontHandle	pla	plx	jsr SetIconFont	Save icon font handle, set parameters.;	rts	EndP************************************************************************ ComputeScrollColor** Look for a good gray in a likely-looking color palette.  If we can't* find one, then use $010F (the old checkerboard pattern).  If we find one,* use $00x0.** We store the new pattern into scroll_color+12, the page color for* the default scroll bar color table.  If we change the value, we* call RefreshDesktop(0) to redraw any scroll bars that happen to be* using the default color table.************************************************************************** 9-Dec-91 DAL -- made this into a proc.  Made it store the new value itself,*** and also refresh the screen if needed.ComputeScrollColor proc export	pha	_GetMasterSCB	pla	and #$0080	beq @320	lda #myScrollPatt640	bra @storeNewValue@320	pha	pea 100	_GetSCB	pla	and #$000f	asl a	asl a	asl a	asl a	asl a	;*32 = index into color stuff	tax	ldy #16@search	lda $e19e00,x	pha	cmp #$0555	;compare against 4 acceptable gray levels	beq @found	cmp #$0666	beq @found	cmp #$0777	beq @found	cmp #$0888	beq @found@noGood	pla	inx	inx	dey	bne @search	lda #$010f	bra @storeNewValue@found	pla	txa	asl a	asl a	asl a	and #$00f0@storeNewValue	cmp >scroll_color+12	sta >scroll_color+12	beq @noChange*** added 14-Jan-92 DAL -- cause a RefreshDesktop to happen later	pushlong #refreshDeskTask	_AddToRunQ*** end 14-Jan-92@noChange	rts*** end 9-Dec-91 DAL*** added 14-Jan-92 DAL** refreshDeskTask -- redraws the desktop once, when it's safe* (this task removes itself from the queue)*	export refreshDeskTaskrefreshDeskTask	dc.l 0	;reserved	dc.w 0	;call as often as possible	dc.w $a55a	;signature	dc.l 0	;reserved for systementry	lda #0	pha	pha	_RefreshDesktop	bcc @fine	cmp #$10	bcs @fine	pla	pla	;clean up after dispatcher error (paranoia)@fine	export RemoveRefreshTaskRemoveRefreshTask	pushlong #refreshDeskTask	_RemoveFromRunQ	rtl*** end 14-Jan-92	ENDP;====================================================================;;          Call SetWAP.;;   IN:    a,y = value to set.;;====================================================================setWAP	proc EXPORT	pea 0	Pass system flag.	pea CtlToolNum	Pass Window Manager	tool number.	phy	Pass value.	pha	_SetWAP		rts	Return error code from SetWAP.		ENDP;====================================================================;;          Allocate	a block of memory.;;   IN:    a = number of bytes to allocate.;          MyID = ID to use.;;  OUT:    Carry clear if handle allocated, a+x = handle.;          Carry set if error, y = error returned by Memory	Manager.;;====================================================================allocate	proc EXPORT	pha	Save number of bytes.	ldy #MyID	Get ID number.	lda [<data],y	tay	y = ID number to use to allocate.	pla	a = number of bytes	to allocate.; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = = = = =;;          Allocate	a block of memory.;;   IN:    y = ID number.;          a = number of bytes.;;  OUT:    Carry clear if handle allocated, a+x = handle.;          Carry set if error, y = error returned by Memory	Manager.;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = = = = =	EXPORT CMAllocate2CMAllocate2		;       	ldx #%0100000000010000 Fixed, May not cross bank boundary.; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = = = = =;;          Allocate	a block of memory.;;   IN:    y = ID number.;          x = attributes.;          a = number of bytes.;;  OUT:    Carry clear if handle allocated, a+x = handle.;          Carry set if error, y = error returned by Memory	Manager.;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = = = = =	EXPORT CMAllocate3CMAllocate3		;       ;	pha	Space for returned handle.	pha	pea 0	High word of size.	pha	Pass low word of size.	phy	Pass ID number.	phx	Pass attributes.	pha	Address doesn't matter.	pha	_NewHandle	pla	Return handle.	plx		rts		ENDP;====================================================================;          Do setup	for tool call.;;   IN:    a+y = handle to data area.;;  OUT:    Carry clear if no error.;          Carry set if null data pointer, y = error code.;;150=================================================================CMstartup	proc EXPORT	plx	Get return address.;	phd	Save caller's direct page.	phb	Save caller's data page.;	phy	Save pointer to data area.	pha;	phx;	pha	Space for result.	pha	_GetPort	pla	ply	plx	Get return addess.	phy	Save caller's port on stack.	pha;	tsc	Allocate direct page on stack.	sec	sbc #DIRECTSIZE	tcs	tcd;	phx	Put return address back on stack.;	lda <data	Valid data area pointer passed.	ora <data+2	clc	Clear error flag.	bne exit;	pea $1002	Control Manager not	started.	pea notInit>>16	Pass message.	pea notInit	_SysFailMgr;notInit	DC.B 40	DC.B 'Control Manager not initialized, error $';exit	rts;;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = =;          Entry points for function exits.;200= = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = =;	EXPORT CMpop0bytesCMpop0bytes		;       	ldx #0	bra shutdown;	EXPORT CMpop4bytesCMpop4bytes		;       	ldx #4	bra shutdown;	EXPORT CMpop6bytesCMpop6bytes		;       	ldx #6	bra shutdown;	EXPORT CMpop8bytesCMpop8bytes		;       	ldx #8	bra shutdown;	EXPORT CMpop10bytesCMpop10bytes		;       	ldx #10	bra shutdown;	EXPORT CMpop12bytesCMpop12bytes		;       	ldx #12	bra shutdown;	EXPORT CMpop18bytesCMpop18bytes		;       	ldx #18	bra shutdown;	EXPORT CMpop26bytesCMpop26bytes		;       	ldx #26	bra shutdown;	EXPORT CMpop32bytesCMpop32bytes		;       	ldx #32	bra shutdown;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = =;;          Undo setup for tool call.;;  IN:     y = error code, zero if no error.;          x = number of bytes to pop.;          Startup must have been called.;;250= = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = =shutdown		; ;	phy	Save error code.	phx	Save number of byte	to pop.	pei <savePort+2	Restore caller's port.	pei <savePort	_SetPort	plx	Restore number of bytes to pop.	ply	Restore error code.;;; --- Restore saved	parameters from startupCall --------------------------;	tsc	Free direct page allocated on stack.	clc	adc #DIRECTSIZE+8	(Get rid of data area pointer and port).	tcs;	plb	Restore original data bank.;;; --- Move return addresses over top of	input parameters -----------------;	tsc	tcd	lda 7,s	sta 7,x	lda 5,s	sta 5,x	lda 3,s	sta 3,x;;; --- Adjust stact for popped parameters ---;	pld	Get original direct	page pointer.;	tsc	Current stack,	phx	clc	adc 1,s	plus number of bytes popped,	tcs	equals new stack.;	tya	Return error code in Y.	cmp #1	Set carry if error.		rtl;;;====================================================================;        ( op1 * op2 ) / op3;;   IN:  x = op1.;        y = op2.;        a = op3.;;  OUT:  x = result.;300=================================================================;	EXPORT fractionfraction	proc export;	pha	Save op3.;	pha	Space for LongDivide remainder high.	pha	Space for LongDivide remainder low.;	pha	Space for LongDivide quotient high.	pha	Space for LongDivide quotient low.;;; --- ( op1 * op2 )	------------------------------;	pha	Space for Multiply result.	pha	Space for Multiply result.;	phx	Pass op1.	phy	Pass op2.	_Multiply;;; --- ( Result ) / op3 ---------------------------;;		Space for result already on stack.;		Numerator is multiply result on stack.	pea 0	Pass high word of op3 as denominator.	lda 11,s	pha	Pass low word of op3 as denominator.	_LongDivide;;; --- Round off quotient --------------------------;	plx	Quotient.	lda 7,s	Get op3.	lsr a	Halve of that.	cmp 3,s	Is it greater that the remainder?	bcs skip300	inx	Round up.;;; --- Fix up stack and exit ------------------------;skip300	pla	Pull quotient high word.	pla	Pull remainder low word.	pla	Pull remainder high	word.;	pla	Pull op3.		rts	x = result.;;;====================================================================;;          Set pen color.;;   IN:    <colorptr = pointer to a color table.;          y = offset into the color table.;;350=================================================================;	EXPORT pen_colorpen_color	proc export;	jsr pushcolor	_SetPenPat		rts;====================================================================;;          Push a pointer to a color patteren.;;   IN:    colorptr	= pointer to a color table.;          y = offset into the color table.;;400=================================================================	EXPORT pushcolorpushcolor	lda [<colorptr],y	and #$00F0	tay	jsr set_patt;	pla	Get return address.;	phx	Push pointer to pattern on stack.	phy;	pha	Restore return address.		rts;====================================================================;;          Push long value in data area.;;460=================================================================	EXPORT pushVdrag_pattpushVdrag_patt		;       	ldy #drag_patt+2	bra enter460;;	EXPORT pushVctl_fontpushVctl_font	proc export	ldy #ctl_font+2;	export enter460enter460	plx	lda [<data],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<data],y	pha	phx		rts;====================================================================;;          Push address of variable in data area.;;470=================================================================;	EXPORT pushrect2pushrect2	proc export	lda #rect2	bra enter470;;	EXPORT pushfontHandlepushfontHandle	proc export	lda #fontHandle	bra enter470;	EXPORT pushfontInfopushfontInfo		;       	lda #fontInfo	bra enter470;	EXPORT pushmyeventpushmyevent		;       	lda #myevent	bra enter470	EXPORT pushmyeventpospushmyeventpos		;       	lda #myevent+where	bra enter470;	EXPORT pushdrag_rectpushdrag_rect		;       	lda #drag_rect	bra enter470;	EXPORT pushbound_rectpushbound_rect		;       	lda #bound_rect	bra enter470;	EXPORT pushslop_rectpushslop_rect		;       	lda #slop_rect	bra enter470;	EXPORT pushlimit_blkpushlimit_blk		;       	lda #limit_blk;enter470	proc export	plx;	clc	adc <data	tay	lda #0	adc <data+2	pha	phy;	phx		rts;====================================================================;;          Push word value from data area.;;480=================================================================;	EXPORT pushVaxis_parampushVaxis_param	proc export	ldy #axis_param	bra enter480;;	EXPORT pushVvert_penpushVvert_pen	proc export	;added PROC 8-Dec-91 DAL	ldy #vert_pen;	export enter480enter480	plx	lda [<data],y	pha	phx		rts;====================================================================;;          Push zero page addresses.;;  OUT:    Y = same	as in.;;500=================================================================	EXPORT pushyratpushyrat;	lda #yrat	bra pushzpage;	EXPORT pushrectpushrect		;       ;	lda #rect;	EXPORT pushzpagepushzpage		;       ;	plx	Get return address.;	pea 0	pha	tdc	clc	adc 1,s	sta 1,s;	phx	Put return address back.		rts;====================================================================;;          Get given window pointer.;;   IN:    Window pointer must be last parameter passed to tool function.;;  OUT:    windptr = pointer to given window.;          ctlhand = handle of first control in window.;          ctlptr =	(ctlptr);          Carry set if error, y = 0.;;550=================================================================;	EXPORT getWindPtrgetWindPtr	proc export	;added PROC 8-Dec-91 DAL;	ldx <inputs+2	Get last input parameter.	lda <inputs	bne ok550	txy	bne ok550;	ldy #0	Don't return an error.	sec		rts;ok550	jsr makeWptr	windptr = window pointer.;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = = = = ;;          Get first control in window.;;   IN:    windptr = pointer to window record.;;  OUT:    ctlhand = handle of first control in window.;          ctlptr =	(ctlptr);          Carry set if no first control found, y = 0.;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = = = = 	EXPORT getFirstCtlgetFirstCtl		;       ;	ldy #owControls+2	Get pointer to first control.	lda [<windptr],y	tax	dey	dey	lda [<windptr],y	bra store550;;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = = = = ;;          Get given control handle.;;   IN:    Control handle must be last parameter passed to tool function.;;  OUT:    ctlhand = handle of first control in window.;          ctlptr =	(ctlptr);          Carry set if null handle passed, y = 0.;;550= = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = = = = 	EXPORT getCtlHandgetCtlHand		;       ;	lda <inputs	ldx <inputs+2;store550	sta <Ctlhand	stx <Ctlhand+2;	ldy #0	No first control found flag, just in case.	sec	ora <Ctlhand+2	Is there a first control?	beq exit550;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	clc	OK flag.;exit550	rts;====================================================================;;          Get window pointer from control.;;   IN:    Ctlptr =	pointer to control.;;  OUT:    windptr = pointer to control's window.;          a = low word of window pointer.;          x = high	word of window pointer.;;600=================================================================	ENTRY get_wptrget_wptr		;       ;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #CtlOwner+2	lda [<Ctlptr],y	tax	dey	dey	lda [<Ctlptr],y;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = =;;          Compute window pointer;          from grafPort pointer.;;   IN:    a,x = pointer to grafPort.;;  OUT:    a,x = pointer to window record.;          windptr = pointer to window record.;;650= = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = =	EXPORT makeWptrmakeWptr		;       	sec	sbc #oport	bcs store650	dexstore650	sta <windptr	stx <windptr+2		rts;====================================================================;;          Switch to window's port.;;   IN:    Ctlptr =	pointer to control.;;  OUT:    current port = Ctlptr's owner (window).;          global_y	= window's Y offset.;          global_x	= window's X offset.;;700=================================================================	EXPORT to_wportto_wport		;       ;; --- Move relevant	data from window port to Control Mgr's port -------------;	jsr dereference	Ctlptr = (Ctlhand).	ldy #CtlOwner+2	Get pointer to window's port.	lda [<Ctlptr],y	pha	dey	dey	lda [<Ctlptr],y	pha	_SetPort;;	                  Fall through to dereference.;; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = =;;          Dereference Ctlhand.;;   IN:    Ctlhand = handle.;;  OUT:    a,x = (Ctlhand);          Ctlptr =	(Ctlhand);;750= = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = =;;;	EXPORT dereferencedereference	proc export;	ldy #2	lda [<Ctlhand],y	sta <Ctlptr+2	tax	lda [<Ctlhand]	sta <Ctlptr		rts; = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = =;;          Push pointer to string.;;   IN:    Ctlhand = handle;          CtlPtr  = ptr;;  OUT:    pointer on stack;;750= = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = = = =	= = = = = = = =;;;	EXPORT PushStringPtrPushStringPtr	proc export	jsr CtlDataToAX	; start by putting value in Ctldata on stack	ply	phx	pha	phy;; If the control is not a super control, we are done.;	ldy #NewCtlRecord.ctlProc+2	lda [ctlPtr],y	bpl @Done;; It is a super control.  See what the verb is.;	jsr ReadMoreFlags	and #TitleVerbMask	beq @Done		0 is pointer so